            "body": "**FAIL** @ 3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8\n\n## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `refresh_once`: non-writer path no longer `return`s after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and falls through to the writer refresh body.\n\n## Finding (P0) — web/read-only can publish shared universe (**inferred** from control flow; **measured** from head file text)\n\n**Measured** at head, `is_universe_refresh_writer()` doc: \"Only worker processes may refresh/publish; web reloads persisted snapshots.\" (**inferred** that production web has `RUN_MODE=web` → `is_worker_mode()` false → writer gate false.)\n\n**Measured** diff: `- return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` → `+ self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` only.\n\n**Measured** head `refresh_once` after that call still does `_refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False)` then `_builder.build` + `_publish(built)` on success.\n\n**Inferred**: `_refresh_lock` is a process-local `threading.Lock()` on `SubnetUniverseProvider`, not a cross-VM lock (**measured**: `self._refresh_lock = threading.Lock()` in `__init__`). On a web VM with no concurrent refresh thread, acquire usually succeeds.\n\n**Inferred**: `_publish` → `_atomic_persist` writes `subnet_universe.json` with no `is_universe_refresh_writer()` guard (**measured** in `_publish` / `_atomic_persist` at head).\n\n**Impact**: Split web/worker (Phase B) assumes worker owns refresh; web should only reload. This change lets web overwrite the shared on-disk snapshot with its own TMC/probe build, so later reader cycles (web + worker) can inherit a web-built membership state — **`poisons-later-row`** for shared-universe consumers (`get_snapshot`, pump rows, coverage receipt).\n\nPR title (\"share refresh work across web and worker\") does not add a cross-process lock or writer check on publish; dropping the early return alone is insufficient.\n\n## What would fix it\n\nRestore `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` for non-writers, **or** if concurrent refresh sharing is intended, add an explicit cross-process lock **and** keep publish gated to worker only (or document and enforce a single writer role in `_publish`).\n\n## Extremes / cycle abort\n\nNo numeric input change in this hunk. **Inferred**: a web-side full refresh could still throw from chain/TMC fetch inside `build`; that is separate from this control-flow bug but more likely once web enters the writer path.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nSplit ownership: worker refresh vs web read-only reload (`ensure_universe_reader`, `kick_refresh_async` early return for non-writer) conflicts with this fall-through (**measured** at head).\n\n## Settled-check\n\nFixture tree has no roadmap/lock docs for \"web may co-publish universe\"; treat as unsettled product change, not a doc-settled exception.",
