      "finalText": "Posted **FAIL** on [PR 9401](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9401) at `3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8`.\n\n### What changed\nThe diff drops the early `return` after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, so the non-writer path can fall through into the full refresh body (lock → `build` → `_publish`).\n\n### Why FAIL (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is documented as worker-only publish; web should reload from disk. **Measured:** `_refresh_lock` is an in-process `threading.Lock()`, not shared across Fly web/worker VMs. **Inferred:** On web, that lock often acquires, so the process can run `_builder.build` and `_atomic_persist` with no writer check in `_publish`.\n\nThat lets a web VM overwrite the shared `subnet_universe.json` and poison what later cycles read (`get_snapshot`, pump membership, coverage receipt)—against Phase B split ownership (`ensure_universe_reader`, non-writer paths in `kick_refresh_async`).\n\nSharing refresh work would need an explicit cross-process coordination story **and** publish still gated to the worker (or a single declared writer)—not just removing the `return`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture session; the formal MC comment is on the PR with the Skills table and blocking list.",
