            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard change in `kick_refresh_async` to treat a non-empty `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` env like the refresh-writer path (spawn daemon thread → `refresh_once()`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` branch is unreachable (**measured**)\n\nAt head, the only call site of `kick_refresh_async` is `ensure_background_refresh()`, and that function calls it **only** when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is already true (web path uses `ensure_universe_reader()` instead). So on `RUN_MODE=web`, nothing in this module ever calls `kick_refresh_async`, and the new env bypass never runs. The PR title (“idle web workers”) is not satisfied by this diff alone.\n\n### P1 — Async thread still does not refresh on web (**measured**)\n\n`refresh_once()` begins with `if not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()`. Even if something later called `kick_refresh_async` on web with `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB`, the background thread would only reload persisted JSON, not run TMC/probe build/publish. That is a different (lighter) behavior than writer refresh unless `refresh_once` is also taught to honor the same flag.\n\n### P2 — Env flag parsing (**inferred** from `run_mode.py` conventions)\n\n`os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` is truthy for any set value, including `\"0\"` and `\"false\"`, unlike `background_on_web()` / `split_worker_v2_enabled()` which use explicit on/off lists. Risk of accidental enable in prod config.\n\n## Adversarial numeric / state review\n\nNo changed numeric inputs (membership grace, probe budget, etc.). Env-only change does not introduce float overflow or membership never-expire paths in the code touched. Web workers still cannot `_publish` via `refresh_once` at head.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nWire web boot to call `kick_refresh_async` when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is enabled (likely in `ensure_background_refresh` or lifespan), align `refresh_once` with the intended writer capability, and parse the flag like other `RUN_MODE` toggles. Until then, this line is dead code in the repo slice reviewed.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced env → kick → refresh_once; writer gate blocks real refresh on web | — |\n| owner-rules | skipped: skill file not readable in this session | — |\n| settled-check | No prior lock found in available files for UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB | — |",
