            "verdict": "FAIL",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: when disk mtime advances, the reader now loads payloads with **empty or missing `netuids`** if `status` is `\"ok\"` or `\"degraded\"`, instead of keeping the in-memory snapshot.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 (P1, blocking) — Empty persisted membership replaces LKG on readers (owner rule 1)\n\n**Measured:** At head, the guard is:\n\n```python\nif not payload.get(\"netuids\") and payload.get(\"status\") not in (\"ok\", \"degraded\"):\n    return self._snapshot\nsnap = UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)\n# ... self._snapshot = snap\n```\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` builds `netuids` only from `payload[\"netuids\"]`; it does **not** reconstruct membership from `validity_map` keys.\n\n**Measured:** `get_netuids()` returns `list(self._snapshot.netuids)`; `load_membership_receipt()` (via `get_snapshot()`) derives `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids`, not from `validity_map` alone.\n\n**Inferred:** A persisted file `{ \"status\": \"ok\"|\"degraded\", \"netuids\": [] }` (with or without a populated `validity_map`) causes web/read-only processes on `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` to **replace** a good in-memory universe with zero members. That blanks shared membership for `/api` and scoring receipts while picks must not go blank (owner rule 1: a snapshot with no members is not complete; the reader must reject it and keep serving the last complete snapshot).\n\n**Inferred:** The worker path can already publish an empty membership snapshot (`status=\"degraded\"`, `netuids=tuple()` — see `SnapshotBuilder.build` empty-membership branch). Before this PR, readers ignored that on reload; after, they honor it — directly opposing fail-closed LKG behavior.\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row` — bad empty membership is written into `self._snapshot` and read by later API/scoring cycles in the same process.\n\n### F2 (P2) — Cold start vs hot reload disagree on the same file\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy before `from_dict`; it does **not** apply the new `status in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")` exception.\n\n**Inferred:** The same compacted/on-disk payload can load as `emergency_registry` on process start but overwrite live LKG after mtime bump on reload, producing inconsistent behavior across restarts.\n\n### F3 (P3) — No test delta in reviewed tree\n\n**Measured:** PR touches only `internal/subnet_universe.py`; no accompanying tests in the available head tree.\n\n## Adversarial trace (reader entry point)\n\n**Measured:** Non-writer `refresh_once()` returns `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`; `ensure_background_refresh()` calls `ensure_universe_reader()` for web. Extreme JSON numeric netuids still fail in `from_dict` and fall back to `self._snapshot` via the existing `except` path — unchanged.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nDo not relax the empty-`netuids` rejection on readers. If worker compaction omits `netuids`, either persist a complete snapshot (non-empty `netuids` or explicit LKG hold) or teach `from_dict` / reload to **rehydrate** `netuids` from `validity_map` and still reject truly empty membership. Align `_load_initial_snapshot` with whatever rule is chosen.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced disk reload → `get_snapshot` / `get_netuids` / membership receipt; empty `netuids` installs blank membership | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 violated: reader accepts incomplete (zero-member) persisted snapshot | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no locks/roadmap/docs in review fixture | — |",
