            "body": "## Summary\n\nNarrow reader-path fix in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the type guard and allow disk reload when `rows` is present even if top-level `netuids` is missing or empty, instead of keeping an in-memory snapshot that predates a row-backed persist file.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Loaded snapshot can have empty `netuids` while `rows` is populated (owner rule 1)\n\n**Measured:** After the new guard, any dict with truthy `rows` and falsy/missing `netuids` calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`, which sets `netuids` only from the `netuids` field (`tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))`) and does not derive membership from `rows` or `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` assigns that snapshot to `_snapshot` with no completeness check.\n\n**Inferred:** `get_netuids()` then returns `[]`, and `get_lkg_or_emergency()` returns `emergency_registry(reason=\"no_usable_snapshot\")` when `not snap.netuids`, rather than retaining the prior in-memory LKG. Owner rule 1 treats empty/zero `netuids` as not a complete persisted snapshot; a reader that adopts it can shrink membership below the last complete snapshot (picks/coverage paths keyed off `snap.netuids`, e.g. `load_membership_receipt()`).\n\n**Suggested fix:** When `rows` (or `validity_map`) is present but top-level `netuids` is empty, derive `netuids` inside `from_dict` (same `_netuid_of` pattern as elsewhere) *or* refuse reload and keep `_snapshot` until `netuids` is non-empty. Align `_load_initial_snapshot` with the same rule for consistency.\n\n### P3 — Startup vs reload asymmetry\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")`; `reload_from_disk_if_stale` now accepts rows-only. **Inferred:** A process can boot into `emergency_registry` on a rows-only file then diverge after mtime reload.\n\n## What looks good\n\n**Measured:** Non-dict JSON still returns prior `_snapshot` without calling `from_dict`. **Measured:** Empty dict with neither `netuids` nor `rows` still skips reload. **Inferred:** Exception path on bad `netuids` types still retains prior snapshot.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced disk reload → `from_dict` → `get_snapshot` / `get_lkg_or_emergency` / membership receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1: empty `netuids` persist shape should not replace a good reader snapshot | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: roadmap/locks not in review fixture | — |",
            "headSha": "92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427",
            "skills": [
              {
                "note": "Traced reload_from_disk_if_stale → from_dict → get_netuids/get_lkg_or_emergency/load_membership_receipt; falsy netuids + truthy rows yields empty membership list.",
