      "sessionId": "ses_4dcee760ecdc4542850ff29e",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [#9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404) at head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427`.\n\nThe reload guard change is aimed in the right direction: when disk has row-backed data but top-level `netuids` is missing or empty, the old path kept a stale in-memory snapshot instead of picking up the file.\n\nThe main issue is completeness on load. **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` only fills `netuids` from the `netuids` field, not from `rows` or `validity_map`. **Inferred:** a reload can install a snapshot with empty `netuids` while `rows` is populated, which makes `get_netuids()` empty and pushes `get_lkg_or_emergency()` to `emergency_registry` instead of retaining the prior LKG — that conflicts with owner rule 1 for netuid-keyed consumers (for example membership receipt / scoring). Recommended follow-up: derive `netuids` when row-backed data is present, or refuse reload until `netuids` is non-empty, and mirror the same rule in `_load_initial_snapshot`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after the post; the formal MC comment is on the PR for this head.",
