            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `9914127` relaxes `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop` so the background thread can start when `inline_worker_expected()` is true even if `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false. CI/test still exits first (**measured**). The loop body still calls `refresh_once()`, which **measured** remains writer-only for build/publish and falls back to `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` on read-only processes — so an inline-worker **web** process would only poll disk, not publish, which is the right safety boundary (**inferred** from `refresh_once` + docstring on `reload_from_disk_if_stale`).\n\n## Guards removed or relaxed (gate)\n\n| Diff hunk | Explanation |\n| --- | --- |\n| `if _ci_or_test() or not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return` → split | **Measured:** `_ci_or_test()` still short-circuits unchanged. Writer check moved into a `try` and becomes `if not is_universe_refresh_writer() and not inline_worker_expected(): return`, i.e. loop allowed when either writer **or** inline-worker web is expected. **Measured:** `except Exception` falls back to writer-only gate if `internal.run_mode` import fails. |\n\nNo overflow / numeric paths touched; no blocking-category defects found in membership math on this diff.\n\n## P2 — PR intent not wired at the boot seam (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` (same module, head) still calls `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true; the `else` branch is `ensure_universe_reader()` (one-shot disk reload, no loop).\n\n**Inferred:** On Fly v1 split (`INLINE_WORKER` on the web machine, `RUN_MODE=web`), boot that uses only `ensure_background_refresh()` never reaches the new `inline_worker_expected()` branch, so the refresh/disk-poll loop still does not start despite the PR title.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Extend `ensure_background_refresh()` (or the lifespan caller **inferred** outside this fixture) so non-writer processes with `inline_worker_expected()` call `get_provider().ensure_refresh_loop()` while keeping `kick_refresh_async()` writer-only.\n\n## P3 — Broad `except Exception` on import path\n\n**Measured:** Any exception from the `try` block (including **inferred** failure inside `inline_worker_expected()`) skips starting the loop unless writer — acceptable fallback, slightly opaque for ops.\n\n## Skills\n\nSee table in verdict tooling.",
