            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `9914127` widens `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop()` so the loop may start when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, not only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true (after the existing CI/test early return).\n\n## Measured\n\n- **`is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (at head): returns `True` only when `RUN_MODE` is worker (except CI/test), per `internal/subnet_universe.py`.\n- **`inline_worker_expected()`** (at head): true when `INLINE_WORKER` is set and `WORKER_SPLIT_V2` is not, on the **web** Fly v1 split layout (`internal/run_mode.py`).\n- **`ensure_background_refresh()`** (at head, unchanged by this PR): calls `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` **only** when `is_universe_refresh_writer()`; otherwise calls `ensure_universe_reader()` (one-shot disk reload).\n- **This PR’s diff**: only relaxes the guard inside `ensure_refresh_loop()`; does not change `ensure_background_refresh()` or any other caller visible in the PR diff.\n- **`refresh_once()`** (at head): if not `is_universe_refresh_writer()`, returns `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — no publish path on web.\n\n## Inferred\n\n- For a web VM with `INLINE_WORKER=1`, the production boot path that **measured** code shows is `ensure_background_refresh()` → `ensure_universe_reader()`, so **`ensure_refresh_loop()` is never invoked** and this PR’s new branch is unreachable unless some other module (not in this PR / not available in review fixture) calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` directly on web.\n- If the loop *were* started on web via this guard, **`refresh_once()` would still behave as a reader** (periodic disk reload), which is coherent for a sibling-worker layout on shared `DATA_DIR`, but only if something actually starts the loop.\n\n## Finding (P2 — wiring)\n\n**Incomplete fix for stated title.** To “start refresh loop when INLINE_WORKER is enabled” on the web process, **`ensure_background_refresh()` (or the real lifespan entry point) likely needs the same `inline_worker_expected()` disjunct** — e.g. start the loop (and optionally keep `kick_refresh_async` writer-only) when inline split expects a co-located worker. As written, the inner guard change alone does not connect INLINE_WORKER to loop startup through the module’s documented boot helper.\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n- Broad `except Exception` around the import falls back to writer-only behavior (**measured**); acceptable defensive pattern here.\n- No float/env numeric hazards in this hunk; no change to membership grace, shrink rules, or scoring admission (**measured** from unchanged paths).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced loop startup from `ensure_background_refresh()` → `ensure_refresh_loop()`; checked `refresh_once()` writer gate | — |\n| owner-rules | Writer-only publish remains in `refresh_once()` / `is_universe_refresh_writer()` | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/lock files in review fixture for this question | skipped: fixture scope |",
