      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [#9405](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9405) at head `9914127cfe0ef5c9ccbd731ae2647e6876cc77fd`.\n\n**Main finding (P2, inferred from measured boot wiring):** The PR relaxes the guard inside `ensure_refresh_loop()` when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, but **`ensure_background_refresh()` still only calls that method when `is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (worker `RUN_MODE`). On a web VM with `INLINE_WORKER=1`, the measured path is `ensure_universe_reader()` only, so the new branch may never run unless something else calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` directly (not shown in this PR).\n\n**Suggested direction:** Mirror the INLINE_WORKER condition at the real boot entry (e.g. `ensure_background_refresh()` or lifespan) so the loop actually starts on inline-split web, while keeping publish gated in `refresh_once()` for non-writers.\n\nNo blocking categories (overflow, never-expires, aborts-cycle, poisons-later-row) were declared for this hunk. Gate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post.",
