          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: accept a persisted dict when `rows` is truthy even if `netuids` is empty/falsy, so startup no longer drops straight to `emergency_registry` for “rows intact, netuids cleared” LKG files.\n\n## Guards removed or relaxed\n\n- **Relaxed** (`internal/subnet_universe.py`): load gate was `payload.get(\"netuids\")`; now `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`. Empty `netuids` with non-empty `rows` now loads via `from_dict` instead of treating the file as unusable.\n\n## Adversarial trace (inferred from code at head)\n\n**Measured:** Diff is exactly the guard above; `from_dict` still sets `netuids` only from `payload[\"netuids\"]` (or `[]`), not from `rows` or `validity_map` keys.\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (web reader path) still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` — unchanged on this head. A rows-only/on-disk snapshot updated after process start is not picked up on reload the way the new initial-load path would accept it.\n\n**Measured:** `get_lkg_or_emergency()` returns `emergency_registry` when `not snap.netuids`, even if `snap.rows` is populated — so callers of that helper still never treat rows-only snapshots as usable LKG.\n\n**Inferred:** If a on-disk file has **cleared `netuids` but intact `validity_map`**, this PR loads it, but the next `SnapshotBuilder.build` uses `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` (empty). Netuids represented only in `prior_map` are not added to `candidates` (`prior_members | observed_members`), so grace/validity state in the map can be dropped on refresh without going through `_eligible_for_removal` — inconsistent with the 48h removal path documented in `_compute_membership`.\n\n**Inferred:** If only `rows` are intact and `validity_map` is empty, refresh rebuilds membership from sources; stale row payloads may be served via `get_pump_membership_rows()` until refresh — lower risk but still a behavioral edge.\n\n## Severity\n\n- **P2:** Align `reload_from_disk_if_stale` with the same accept predicate (or derive membership from rows/map on load) so worker/web paths agree.\n- **P2:** On load, reconcile `netuids` from `validity_map` keys and/or row `netuid` fields before refresh consumes the snapshot (or document that cleared-netuids files must also clear `validity_map`).\n- **P3:** `get_lkg_or_emergency` vs `_load_initial_snapshot` intent — clarify whether rows-only snapshots are meant to satisfy “LKG” for all entry points.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nThe relaxed guard is directionally right for the PR title, but accepting the file without reconciling membership fields can let refresh **inherit bad prior state** (validity without `prior_members`). MODIFY to tighten load/reload symmetry and membership reconstruction; not a one-line PASS.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Load → `from_dict` → `build(prior)`; empty `prior.netuids` + nonempty map | — |\n| owner-rules | 48h removal / chain-wins semantics assume prior membership is carried via `prior.netuids` | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture repo for this LKG shape | skipped: no settled docs in session fixture |",
