            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change widens `_load_initial_snapshot` so persisted LKG is accepted when `rows` is present even if `netuids` is cleared (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). Direction matches the PR title; the load gate alone is not enough for a safe end-to-end path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Refresh can wipe a rows-only LKG the PR now loads (**P2**, **blocking: poisons-later-row**)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` (head) accepts `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))` and calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`, which sets `netuids` from the `netuids` field only (`tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))`) and keeps `rows` from `rows` (`from_dict`, ~lines 481–494).\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` seeds `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` only—not from `prior.rows` or `validity_map` keys (~lines 551–552).\n\n**Inferred:** For a file with cleared `netuids` but non-empty `rows`, after this change the worker retains those rows in memory. On the next `refresh_once` → `build`, if `_compute_membership` yields an empty `netuids` list but `had_verified_resolution` is true (e.g. non-empty `prior_map` from disk plus `tmc_complete` or `probe_complete`), the branch at ~lines 604–616 publishes `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=tuple(), rows=tuple(), …)` via `_publish`—**dropping the intact rows** that motivated the fix. Before this PR, the same file never entered that state at startup (it fell through to `emergency_registry`).\n\n**Suggested fix (minimal):** When `netuids` is empty after load, derive membership candidates from row `netuid` fields and/or `validity_map` keys inside `from_dict` or at the start of `build`; and/or extend the `_hold_prior` path when `prior.rows` is non-empty and refresh would publish empty rows. Align `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (~line 681) with the same accept predicate so web readers pick up the same LKG shape.\n\n### 2. Reader reload still rejects rows-only disk files (**P3**, non-blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (~line 681). **Inferred:** Web/read-only processes will not adopt a worker-persisted rows-only snapshot even after cold-start load succeeds on the writer.\n\n### 3. `get_lkg_or_emergency` still treats empty `netuids` as unusable (**P3**, non-blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `get_lkg_or_emergency` returns `emergency_registry` when `not snap.netuids` (~lines 778–781). **Inferred:** Callers using that helper still ignore a loaded rows-only snapshot; pump paths using `get_pump_membership_rows` / `get_snapshot` may see rows until a refresh overwrites them (finding 1).\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n**Measured:** Invalid `netuids` entries that break `int(n)` in `from_dict` still land in the broad `except` → `lkg_corrupt` → `emergency_registry`. No new float/`inf` surface in this diff.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nChange is appropriately minimal in diff size; owner chain-wins / grace semantics in `_merge_sources` are untouched. Accepting partial LKG without reconciling refresh/read paths conflicts with retaining last-known-good row data across cycles.\n\n## Settled-check\n\nNo roadmap/docs in the available repo snapshot for “cleared netuids, intact rows”; not treated as settled—finding 1 is new scope for this head.",
