            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: accept a persisted dict when `netuids` is empty/falsy but `rows` is present, instead of falling through to `emergency_registry`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Reader reload still rejects the same files (**measured**)\n\n`reload_from_disk_if_stale` (web/read-only path via `ensure_universe_reader`) still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` at head. Only `_load_initial_snapshot` was updated. A running reader that already holds an in-memory snapshot will **not** pick up a worker-published file in the “cleared `netuids`, intact `rows`” shape; cold start will. If the fix is meant for live disk reload as well as process boot, mirror the same predicate on the reload path.\n\n### P2 — Guard treats any truthy `rows` as usable (**inferred**)\n\nCondition is `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`. A non-list truthy `rows` value (e.g. string) passes the guard; `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` then yields empty `rows` and empty `netuids`. **Measured:** `get_pump_membership_rows()` returns `[]` when `snap.rows` is empty; **inferred:** that is a blank pump row surface versus the prior path (emergency registry rows). Prefer `isinstance(payload.get(\"rows\"), list) and payload[\"rows\"]` or reject after `from_dict` unless `snap.rows` or `snap.netuids` is non-empty.\n\n### P3 — Owner rule 1 vs stated intent (**inferred**)\n\nStanding rule 1 rejects persisted snapshots with zero members. This PR explicitly accepts them when `rows` remain. **Measured:** `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still returns `emergency_registry` when `not snap.netuids`, so LKG-gated callers stay fail-closed; **inferred:** pump/API paths using `get_snapshot()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still serve persisted `rows` while membership receipts stay empty (`expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` only in `load_membership_receipt`). That matches the PR title but should be documented so picks readers are not assumed to use the loaded empty-`netuids` snapshot as “complete.”\n\n### P3 — `netuids` / `validity_map` desync (**inferred**)\n\n`from_dict` does not rebuild `netuids` from `rows` or `validity_map` keys. A file with cleared `netuids` but non-empty `rows` (and possibly stale `validity_map`) loads with empty membership until a writer refresh. Acceptable if that transient is the bug being fixed; if not, reconcile on load.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n- `netuids: []`, `rows: []` — falsy guard; still falls through to emergency (**measured**).\n- `1e308` / float edge cases — not in this diff path (**skipped** for this one-line JSON gate).\n\n## Conclusion\n\nDirection aligns with the PR title and preserves persisted row payloads on cold start instead of registry emergency. Ship after tightening the `rows` type guard and aligning `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (or documenting why reload must stay strict).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Reload asymmetry; truthy non-list `rows`; consumer split (`get_lkg_or_emergency` vs `get_pump_membership_rows`) | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 tension acknowledged; LKG path still rejects empty `netuids` | — |\n| settled-check | PR title settles intent for rows-accompanied LKG; reload parity not settled in diff | — |",
