          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `e6194fed` replaces inline `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_f2_netuids_a(validity_map)` in `_compute_membership`, filtering keys with `if int(k)` (drops netuid **0**). **Measured** from `internal/subnet_universe.py` and the PR patch.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Unsafe-shrink guard blocks the intended alignment on existing LKG (**measured**)\n\n`refresh_once` refuses to publish when `_shrink_allowed` is false. That helper requires every netuid in `prior.netuids − build.snapshot.netuids` to appear in `build.dropped` with removal evidence. Netuid **0** is never dropped via `_eligible_for_removal` (ROOT is protected) and is only omitted from `build.snapshot.netuids` by the new filter.\n\nAny persisted snapshot that still has `0 ∈ netuids` ( **inferred** common when `validity_map` held `\"0\"` under the old extractor) will hit “Unsafe shrink blocked — retained last-known-good universe” on every refresh. The worker keeps publishing the old list; the helper’s filtered list never lands. The PR title’s alignment does not apply on upgrade until shrink policy treats root list omission separately.\n\n### P2 — Snapshot can pair empty `netuids` with non-empty `validity_map` (**inferred**)\n\nIf `validity_map` contains only `\"0\"` (e.g. `prior_members={0}` and no other positive candidates), `r1b_f2_netuids_a` returns `[]` while the map still holds an entry. `SnapshotBuilder.build` then takes the `if not netuids:` branch and can publish `netuids=()` with a non-empty `validity_map` and empty `rows` — downstream `/api/subnets`, pump rows, and `get_lkg_or_emergency()` see an empty universe while validity metadata says otherwise.\n\n### P3 — Helper placement and naming (**inferred**)\n\n`r1b_f2_netuids_a` lives in `internal/run_mode.py` (Fly mode flags) and is imported inside the hot membership loop. The name does not describe behavior (`membership_netuids_from_validity_map` / living next to `ROOT_NETUID` would match `snapshot_coverage.membership_scoring_expected`, which already uses `int(n) > 0`).\n\n## Extremes / numeric seam\n\nNot applicable — no new float env inputs or TTL math in this diff.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**MODIFY**: (1) teach shrink/publish that omitting `ROOT_NETUID` from `netuids` is not an evidence-backed removal, or strip `0` in `_shrink_allowed` when comparing; (2) guard the empty-`netuids` publish path when `validity_map` is non-empty; (3) move/rename the helper beside universe membership and use an explicit `int(k) > 0` (or shared helper with `snapshot_coverage`).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `netuids` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `refresh_once` / `_shrink_allowed` / `get_lkg_or_emergency`; root filter vs drop evidence | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain/grace rules unchanged; membership list should stay consistent with scoring receipts (`int(n) > 0`) | — |\n| settled-check | No fixture docs/locks in session; did not treat root-in-`netuids` vs scoring-only exclusion as settled | — |",
