      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9407](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9407) at head `e6194fed7d8ffb289adee21bb5c9d2af11f879a4`.\n\nThe change routes membership IDs through `r1b_f2_netuids_a`, which drops netuid **0** via `if int(k)`. Two issues drove MODIFY (with **poisons-later-row** declared for the empty-list case):\n\n1. **Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` treats removing `0` from `netuids` like any other shrink and demands drop evidence. Root is never in `dropped`, so any LKG that still lists `0` will keep getting “Unsafe shrink blocked” and the new extractor never publishes on upgrade.\n\n2. **Inferred:** If `validity_map` only has `\"0\"`, the helper returns `[]` while the map stays non-empty, so `build()` can publish empty `netuids`/rows with validity metadata still present.\n\nAlso noted: helper name/placement in `run_mode.py` and a lazy import inside `_compute_membership`; align with `snapshot_coverage`’s explicit `int(n) > 0` pattern.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the session fixture after post; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps were not run in this session.",
