            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_f2_netuids_b(validity_map)` in `_compute_membership`. The helper filters with `if k`, which **drops netuid 0** even when root remains a positive member in `validity_map`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Root dropped from `netuids` while still in `validity_map` (**inferred** from head code)\n\n`_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` to candidates when `observed_members` is non-empty, still writes `\"0\"` into `validity_map`, and `_eligible_for_removal` still refuses to remove root. The old line included every validity-map key in `netuids`, including 0.\n\nNew helper in `internal/subnets/tradable.py`:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_b(validity_map):\n    return sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map.keys()) if k)\n```\n\n`if k` is false for `k == 0`, so published snapshots can carry `validity_map[\"0\"]` while `snap.netuids` omits 0.\n\n**Owner rule 3:** netuid 0 is never removed from membership; this change removes it from the membership list output.\n\n**Downstream:** `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` (**measured** in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`) — that flag would go false despite root still being merged into `validity_map`.\n\n**Shrink path:** If prior LKG included 0 and the new build omits it without a `dropped[0]` entry, `_shrink_allowed` treats the drop as unsafe and may hold prior (**inferred**). Fresh or non-root priors can still persist the inconsistent map/list split (**inferred**).\n\n### P3 — Wrong abstraction layer (**inferred**)\n\n`tradable.py` documents root as excluded from **tradable picks** (`is_tradable_subnet`: `n > 0`). Shared universe membership explicitly documents the opposite for root (`ROOT_NETUID` comment: membership adds it). Reusing a tradable-style filter for universe `netuids` conflates two settled semantics.\n\n### Not raised as blocking\n\n- `int(x)` on bad keys still raises and can abort the cycle — same as before (**inferred**).\n- Late import inside `_compute_membership` — style only.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nIf the goal is deduplication/sorting only, keep parity with the prior line (include 0). If the goal is tradable-only IDs, stop writing root into `validity_map` for universe membership and reconcile owner rule 3 + receipt telemetry explicitly — do not silently filter only at list construction.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `r1b_f2_netuids_b` → `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` / persist / `root_netuid_in_membership`; `if k` removes 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 (netuid 0 never removed); rule 2 N/A | — |\n| settled-check | Prior art: `ROOT_NETUID` membership comment + `root_netuid_in_membership` receipt field expect 0 may appear in `snap.netuids`; tradable `n>0` is for scoring/picks, not this list | — |",
