      "finalText": "**FAIL** posted on [PR 9410](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9410) at head `bca36052f6be11c67b52c733747a7373cf2ff74a`.\n\n### Why FAIL (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe new helper `r1b_f2_netuids_d` ends with `sorted(x for x in keys if x)`. In Python, `if x` is false for netuid **0**, so root is removed from the exported `netuids` list even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** Base code used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which includes 0. Head still defines `ROOT_NETUID = 0`, still adds root to candidates/membership, and `_eligible_for_removal` still forbids dropping root—but the list handed to `SnapshotBuilder.build`, `_build_rows`, persistence, and `get_netuids()` can omit 0. That mismatch can be written to disk and read back on later cycles.\n\n**Owner rule 3:** Netuid 0 must never be removed from the universe; this change effectively drops it from the served membership list.\n\n### Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → snapshot publish; `if x` drops 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 violated | — |\n| settled-check | No settled override for this helper in fixture | — |\n\n**Fix:** Sort all validity-map keys (include 0), or keep root explicitly—do not reuse chain-style “exclude 0” filtering on universe export lists.\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review`; formal FAIL is on the PR via `post_verdict`. Author should fix and push a new head before the gate can advance.",
