k)` removes 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Root membership is explicit (`ROOT_NETUID`, `candidates.add`); scoring layers already use `int(n) > 0` separately — do not silently drop 0 only at this line | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture repo slice; duplicate-int-from-keys dedupe is not a settled exclusion of netuid 0 | — |\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nMODIFY: the dedupe/normalize intent is sound, but `if int(k)` is the wrong filter and creates inconsistent snapshot shape. Not PASS while `poisons-later-row` applies.",
