            ],
            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `internal.run_mode.r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a`. The helper is not a pure move: it adds `if int(k)`, which drops netuid **0** from `netuids` while `_compute_membership` can still write `validity_map[\"0\"]` whenever `observed_members` is non-empty (`candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `netuids` vs `validity_map` divergence (blocking)\n\n**Measured:** At base, `_compute_membership` ended with `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (includes 0 when the map has `\"0\"`). At head, `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` returns `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, excluding 0.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` and, when `observed_members` is truthy, the loop still adds root to `candidates` and can persist a `\"0\"` entry in `validity_map` (root cannot pass `_eligible_for_removal`).\n\n**Inferred:** A published `UniverseSnapshot` can therefore carry `validity_map[\"0\"]` while `netuids` omits 0. Downstream code treats those fields differently (`universe_snapshot_feed_meta` counts `validity_map` entries vs `len(snap.netuids)`; `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`). That inconsistent disk state is readable on later refresh cycles → **poisons-later-row**.\n\n### P2 — Unsafe-shrink interaction on upgrade\n\n**Inferred:** If a persisted LKG still lists `0` in `prior.netuids`, a head build that omits 0 cannot attach `DropEvidence` for root (`_eligible_for_removal` is false for `ROOT_NETUID`). `_shrink_allowed` would block the shrink and `_hold_prior` every refresh until manual intervention — behavior change not covered in the diff.\n\n### P3 — Placement / import\n\n**Inferred:** `run_mode.py` is process-mode configuration; subnet membership projection belongs beside universe code (or a shared membership module). Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` adds coupling on every membership resolution.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**Measured:** Map keys are `str(netuid)` from the membership loop — not arbitrary user strings — so `int(k)` does not introduce new parse hazards vs the old comprehension.\n\n**Measured:** No float/`1e308`/NaN path in this diff.\n\n## Ask\n\nEither (a) keep 0 in `netuids` when it remains in `validity_map` (preserve base behavior), or (b) drop root from `validity_map` at the same boundary and add an explicit migration/shrink story for LKG rows that still list 0. Add a focused unit test for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` (map with `\"0\"` + positive netuids).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → helper → `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` / persist / `_shrink_allowed`; confirmed `if int(k)` excludes 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Applied inline owner rules in `_merge_sources` (chain wins); could not load SKILL.md in this fixture | — |\n| settled-check | No docs/locks in fixture for r1b; treated divergence as open | — |",
