> 0` like `is_tradable_subnet`; behavior matches for normal keys, but naming/clarity could mirror `is_tradable_subnet`.\n- **P3:** No test in this diff for helper or shrink interaction (fixture tree has no pytest here).\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n**Measured:** Invalid `validity_map` keys still raise on `int(k)` (same as base). No new float/NaN path. Root filter does not affect grace/removal clocks in `validity_map`.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nNo change to chain-wins merge, 48h grace, or worker-only refresh writer seam.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced map → helper → `netuids` → `_build_rows` / shrink gate; root exclusion triggers LKG hold | — |\n| owner-rules | Aligns with tradable Root exclusion and receipt telemetry | — |\n| settled-check | Root-not-in-tradable-universe is already documented in `tradable.py` and scoring filters; shrink coupling is not settled and is introduced by this diff | — |",
