      "finalText": "**Verdict: FAIL** posted for head `265a4b46f9dc54e3a7cd7f372235f248139050c3`.\n\nThe change replaces a straight `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c`, which uses `if int(k)` and therefore **drops netuid 0**. Base code and `ROOT_NETUID = 0` keep root in membership when it is in `validity_map`; `_eligible_for_removal` already forbids removing it.\n\n**Measured:** On head, `_compute_membership` can leave `\"0\"` in `validity_map` while `netuids` and `_build_rows` omit 0, so persisted snapshots disagree with themselves and downstream code that checks `0 in snap.netuids` (e.g. council membership receipt) sees root missing.\n\n**Settled:** `snapshot_coverage.py` already excludes 0 only for **scoring** (`int(n) > 0`), not for universe `netuids`. Putting a truthiness filter in `score_cache` and calling it from `subnet_universe` crosses that boundary.\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row` (owner rule 3).\n\nFix: any shared helper must include **all** validity_map keys, including 0, or keep separate membership vs scoring helpers.",
