            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor extracts netuid list construction into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c`, but the helper is **not** behavior-preserving versus base.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Semantic change: netuid 0 dropped from `netuids` (**inferred** from diff + read at head)\n\nBase (`_compute_membership`):\n\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`\n\nHead helper (`internal/council/score_cache.py`):\n\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`\n\nThe `if int(k)` guard removes **ROOT_NETUID (0)** whenever `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`. That path is reachable: `_compute_membership` adds `ROOT_NETUID` to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty (measured in `internal/subnet_universe.py`), and root is never eligible for removal (`_eligible_for_removal` returns false for 0).\n\n**Consumers traced (inferred):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` → `get_netuids()`, `/api/subnets` rows via `_build_rows(netuids, …)`, pump membership (`get_pump_membership_rows`), and coverage receipt field `root_netuid_in_membership` (`0 in snap.netuids` in `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt`).\n\nEffects:\n\n1. **Map/list split:** `validity_map` can still contain `\"0\"` while `netuids` omits 0 on the same snapshot.\n2. **Telemetry drift:** `root_netuid_in_membership` would read false even when root validity was just written — opposite of historical behavior when root was listed in `netuids`.\n3. **Shrink guard (inferred):** If persisted LKG already has `0 in prior.netuids`, a head build that omits 0 without a `dropped[0]` entry fails `_shrink_allowed` (root cannot satisfy removal evidence), forcing `_hold_prior` and a degraded retain — extra churn on upgrade, not documented in the PR.\n\nScoring already excludes root via `membership_scoring_expected(..., if int(n) > 0)` (measured in `snapshot_coverage.py`); this change alters the **published universe list**, not just scoring, without an in-diff justification.\n\n### P3 — Module placement + lazy import (**inferred**)\n\n- Membership derivation lives in `score_cache.py` (TTL scoring cache), which obscures the D5 universe seam.\n- `from internal.council.score_cache import …` inside `_compute_membership` adds a per-refresh import on the writer hot path.\n\nNeither is blocking alone; fix together with semantics.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nEither:\n\n- Match base exactly: `return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` inside the shared helper, **or**\n- If excluding root from `netuids` while keeping `validity_map[\"0\"]` is intentional, state that in the PR, add/adjust tests for root + shrink + `root_netuid_in_membership`, and consider a dedicated module (not `score_cache`).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → helper → `build` → persisted snapshot / API netuids; `if int(k)` excludes 0 vs base | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins / root probe skip unchanged; no new overflow/TTL paths | — |\n| settled-check | Coverage already tracks `root_netuid_in_membership`; this diff changes that signal without a visible settled doc in-repo (fixture) | — |\n\nNo measured overflow, never-expires, or cycle-abort via float extremes in this diff.",
