      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9454 at head `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d` (blocking: `poisons-later-row`).\n\n### Finding\n\nThe new helper is not a pure refactor:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f(validity_map):\n    return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\n**Measured:** Base `_compute_membership` used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which includes netuid **0** when `\"0\"` is in the map.\n\n**Inferred:** `if int(k)` is falsy for `0`, so **0 is dropped** from `netuids` even when `_compute_membership` still puts root in `validity_map` (`ROOT_NETUID = 0`, added when `observed_members` is non-empty; root cannot be dropped via `_eligible_for_removal`).\n\nThat flows through `SnapshotBuilder.build` into persisted `snap.netuids` / rows and into `load_membership_receipt()` (`root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`). You can get **`validity_map[\"0\"]` without 0 in netuids or rows** — inconsistent state for later cycles (**owner rule 3**).\n\n### Ask\n\nUse an explicit predicate (e.g. `int(k) > 0` only if that is intended), or keep **0** in the universe list like base; align `validity_map` / receipts if root is deliberately excluded; add a test with `\"0\"` in the map.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced map → helper → snapshot persist / receipts; falsy filter drops 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 | — |\n| settled-check | Base included 0; scoring `> 0` is a separate path | — |",
