Measured:** Title: \"ci: run universe tests on every shard\". Changed files in this head: `pytest.ini`, `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` only (no workflow/shard wiring in the fixture tree). **Inferred:** CI shard changes may live outside this snapshot; if they are in the real PR, link them in the description so reviewers see the full mechanism (which shard runs what, and how deselect/skip interact with sharding).\n\n## Adversarial numeric / persistence trace\n\n**Measured:** This diff does not modify `internal/subnet_universe.py` or runtime merge/removal paths. Extreme-value and overflow tracing **skipped:** no new accepted numeric inputs in production code on this head.\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone declared: the change does not introduce new production paths for never-expire, overflow-to-inf, cycle abort, or cross-row poison on this head. Risk here is **inferred** test-coverage regression, not a measured logic defect in shipped code.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced T1/T9 through `SnapshotBuilder.build` / `_merge_sources` at head; no prod diff to push extremes through | — |\n| owner-rules | T9 + T1 docstrings encode chain-wins and no-fabricated-universe rules; global skip/deselect weakens CI enforcement | — |\n| settled-check | No locks/docs in fixture repo proving universe tests must be globally skipped/deselected | — |",
