            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe PR adds `_token_count_guard` and an early exit in `_eligible_for_removal`, but the guard is invoked with the constant `0`, so it always fails and **no netuid can ever become eligible for removal**. That breaks the existing 48h grace + chain-negative removal path and forces unsafe-shrink holds every cycle a drop is attempted.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P0 — Removal gate wired to constant zero (**measured**)\n\nAt head, `_eligible_for_removal` begins with:\n\n```python\nif not _token_count_guard(0):\n    return False\n```\n\nand `_token_count_guard` returns `token_count > 0`. With argument `0`, the guard is always false, so `_eligible_for_removal` always returns false before the existing probe / `negative_since` / grace checks.\n\n**Consumers (inferred from reading the module):**\n\n- `_compute_membership` only records `dropped[netuid]` when `_eligible_for_removal` is true — drops never accumulate.\n- `_shrink_allowed` requires `_eligible_for_removal` for every netuid leaving the prior set — shrink is blocked and `_hold_prior` retains the last-known-good universe (`refresh_once`).\n\nSo chain-negative netuids that should leave membership after `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` instead **never expire** from the persisted universe and **poison later refresh cycles** (stale netuids keep flowing to pump rows, validity_map, and downstream membership receipts).\n\nThis contradicts the PR title (“gate removals on **token_count** for audit trails”): `DropEvidence` still has only `tmc`, `probe`, and `negative_since` — no token_count is read or passed (**measured**).\n\n### P1 — Possible invalid function signature (**inferred**)\n\nThe head file text shows `def _token_count_guard(token_count=<redacted> -> bool:` without a visible closing `)` before `->`. If that is literal source (not an artifact of redaction), the module would not import and any cycle touching `internal.subnet_universe` would abort. I did not execute Python here; treat as **inferred** pending author confirmation.\n\n## What would fix it\n\n- Pass the audit-trail token count (or a boolean derived from persisted audit state) into the guard — not the literal `0`.\n- Ensure the guard gates only the intended audit-trail case and still allows the established probe-false + grace removal path.\n- Add/adjust tests for eligible vs blocked removal with token_count present/absent.\n\n## Extremes not run\n\nNo shell/pytest in this session — behavior conclusions from static trace only (**inferred**).",
