      "finalText": "Posted **FAIL** on PR 9440 at `2dbb5f5e435c4aa2b6a6e0497d80367e1beea7bd`.\n\n### Blocking finding (**measured**)\n\n`_eligible_for_removal` now starts with `if not _token_count_guard(0): return False`, while `_token_count_guard` returns `token_count > 0`. The argument is always **0**, so the guard always fails and **every** removal is rejected before the existing probe-false, `negative_since`, and 48h grace logic runs.\n\nThat breaks the real entry path: `_compute_membership` never records drops, `_shrink_allowed` blocks shrink, and `refresh_once` keeps holding the prior universe—so chain-negative netuids **never leave** membership after grace and **stale netuids carry forward** into later cycles (pump rows, validity_map, membership receipts).\n\nThe PR title mentions gating on **token_count** for audit trails, but **`DropEvidence` still has no `token_count`** and nothing from an audit trail is passed into the guard (**measured**).\n\n### Verdict\n\n**FAIL** with blocking tags: `never-expires`, `poisons-later-row`.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Constant-zero guard blocks all removals via `_compute_membership` / `_shrink_allowed` | — |\n| owner-rules | Conflicts with chain-negative + grace shrink semantics already documented nearby | — |\n| settled-check | No settled waiver for disabling removal eligibility | — |\n\n**Fix direction:** Wire the guard to the actual audit-trail token count (or derived flag), not literal `0`, and keep the established grace removal path working; add tests for allowed vs blocked removal.",
