            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `a34965c9` adds `_api_key_present()` and gates default `probe_val` for netuids missing from `probe_map` while `probe_complete` is false:\n\n- **Measured:** With a non-blank `TMC_API_KEY` env, behavior matches base (`probe_val = None`).\n- **Measured:** Without that env, missing map entries become `probe_val = False`.\n- **Measured:** PR title references an `api_key` **header**; the diff only reads `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` inside `_compute_membership` — no header plumbing in the changed file or the fixture tree.\n\n## Entry point\n\n**Measured:** Production refresh path is `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources` → persisted `validity_map` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Incomplete probe + no `TMC_API_KEY` writes chain-negative for unobserved netuids (blocking)\n\n**Measured:** When `not probe_complete` and `netuid not in probe_map`, the new else branch sets `probe_val = False`.\n\n**Measured:** `_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is not False` as chain-negative immediately (`\"negative\"`, sets `negative_since`) — and `tmc_positive is None` satisfies `is not False`.\n\n**Inferred:** Typical partial probe (deadline, RPC failure) leaves many candidates off `probe_map` while `tmc_complete` is still false (`SnapshotBuilder.build` uses `range(MAX_NETUIDS)` when TMC incomplete). Workers without `TMC_API_KEY` then stamp those slots negative in `validity_map`, which is persisted and read by later refreshes and by `load_membership_receipt` / scoring gates — bad state that outlives the failed cycle.\n\n**Measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` docstring says a failed/incomplete chain read should not observe membership and should keep prior members; synthesizing `False` for gaps under incomplete probe contradicts that for the no-key case.\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row`\n\n### P2 — Title/intent vs signal source\n\n**Inferred:** If the intended fix is “do not treat pagination/TMC gaps as chain gaps when the caller supplied an API key **header**”, env-only gating in the worker may miss the web/request path or mislead operators who set headers but not env.\n\n**Suggested direction:** Gate gap-as-False on `probe_complete` and/or explicit chain evidence; align key detection with wherever TMC auth actually enters (header vs env); add regression tests for partial `probe_map` with and without key.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Partial probe + empty `TMC_API_KEY` → mass `probe_val=False` → negative validity persisted | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins branch fires on synthetic `False` while sources incomplete | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: skill file not readable in this session environment | — |",
            "headSha": "a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e",
