      "sessionId": "ses_70b5424c699069e8c384c078",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9442](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9442) at head `a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e`.\n\n**Headline:** When `probe_complete` is false and a netuid is missing from `probe_map`, the branch without `TMC_API_KEY` sets `probe_val = False`. **Measured:** `_merge_sources` then treats that as chain-negative even when `tmc_positive` is `None`, which **inferred** can persist incorrect `\"negative\"` rows across refreshes after a partial probe (deadline/RPC failure)—declared blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Secondary:** The title mentions an `api_key` **header**, but **measured** the diff only checks `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")`; no header wiring appears in the changed file or this fixture tree.\n\n**What would unblock:** Do not synthesize chain `False` for probe gaps while the chain read is incomplete (or narrow the no-key branch); align key detection with the real TMC auth path; add tests for partial `probe_map` with/without key.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; formal MC comment is on the PR with the skills table.",
