          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change in `_compute_membership`: adds `_api_key_present()` and, when `probe_complete` is false and a netuid is absent from `probe_map`, sets `probe_val` to `None` if `TMC_API_KEY` is present in the environment, otherwise `False`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Incomplete probe gaps synthesized as chain negatives without API key (**inferred**, **poisons-later-row**)\n\n**Measured:** At base, the branch always assigned `probe_val = None`. At head, when `_api_key_present(os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\"))` is false, missing map entries become `probe_val = False` while `probe_complete` is still false.\n\n**Measured:** `_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` with `tmc_positive is not False` as the owner “chain wins” path: validity `negative`, `negative_since` stamped, comment references a *complete* chain read — but there is no guard on `probe_complete` in that branch.\n\n**Inferred:** Any refresh where the registration probe returns incomplete with a sparse or empty `probe_map` (e.g. `_default_probe_fetch` → `{}, False` on head pin failure or deadline) will assign synthetic `False` to every candidate netuid not present in the map **when `TMC_API_KEY` is unset**. That starts or continues negative grace and can drive `_eligible_for_removal` (requires `evidence.probe is False`) after 48h — i.e. shrink membership on evidence that was never observed, contradicting the probe helper docstring that incomplete reads should not observe registration.\n\n**Measured:** When `TMC_API_KEY` *is* present, behavior for this branch matches base (`None`) — the fix targets keyed deployments only; the `else False` path is a new regression vs base for unkeyed environments (local dev, CI without secret, misconfigured worker).\n\n### P2 — PR title vs implementation (**measured** / **guess**)\n\nTitle references an `api_key` **header**; code only inspects `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")`. **Guess:** production may inject the header into env on the worker, but this diff does not show that wiring — universe refresh cannot read per-request headers here.\n\n### P3 — No tests in diff (**measured**)\n\nNo accompanying test changes in this PR (fixture shows only `internal/subnet_universe.py`). Behavior change for gap filling under incomplete probe should have a table-driven test for: keyed vs unkeyed env, empty vs partial `probe_map`, `probe_complete=False`.\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**Skipped:** fixture checkout has no docs/locks/tests for prior decisions on TMC gap semantics; could not re-litigate from repo artifacts.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nKeep the keyed path (`None` when API key present). Drop or invert the `else False` branch so incomplete probe never fabricates `False` (restore base `None` for unkeyed), **or** gate the chain-wins branch on `probe_complete` inside `_merge_sources` / only pass `False` when probe actually observed the netuid. Add tests before merge.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `probe_val` → `_merge_sources` → `DropEvidence` / `_eligible_for_removal`; empty incomplete `probe_map` + missing `TMC_API_KEY` → mass synthetic negatives | — |\n| owner-rules | “Chain wins” applies to definitive chain reads; incomplete probe should not assert unregistered | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in minimal fixture | skipped: no roadmap/tests in session fixture |",
            "blocking": [
