      "sessionId": "ses_d54a7898be5918d17be1c553",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9442 at `a34965c9`.\n\n### Verdict\n\nThe keyed path is sensible: when `TMC_API_KEY` is set and the registration probe is incomplete, netuids missing from `probe_map` still get `probe_val = None`, same as base — so TMC gap scans do not invent chain negatives.\n\nThe **`else False` branch is the problem** (**inferred**, blocking **`poisons-later-row`**). If the env key is absent while `probe_complete` is false, every netuid not in `probe_map` is treated as `probe_positive=False`. `_merge_sources` then runs the “chain wins” negative path (comment says *complete* chain read, but nothing checks `probe_complete`). An empty or failed probe (`{}, False`) can stamp `negative_since` across prior members and, after the 48h grace, drive removals on evidence that was never observed — a regression vs base, which always used `None` here.\n\nSecondary notes (**measured**): the title mentions an `api_key` header, but the diff only reads `TMC_API_KEY` from the environment; there are no test changes in this PR.\n\n### Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Incomplete probe + missing env key → synthetic `False` → merge/removal | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins path should not run on incomplete probe synthesis | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture has no prior policy docs | — |\n\n**Recommendation:** Keep `None` when the key is present; remove or fix the unkeyed `False` path (or only assert `False` when the probe actually observed the netuid), and add table tests for keyed/unkeyed × incomplete probe × sparse map.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the session fixture (MC verdict may not persist there); Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow your usual gate order on GitHub.",
