            "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds `_bearer_ok` and gates `_eligible_for_removal` on `os.environ.get(\"AUTH_BEARER\")` before the existing probe / 48h-grace checks. **Measured** entry path: worker `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once()` → `SnapshotBuilder.build()` → `_compute_membership()` / `_shrink_allowed()` → `_eligible_for_removal()`.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Sev | Finding | Label |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| P2 | `_bearer_ok(None)` returns **True**, so when `AUTH_BEARER` is **unset** removal eligibility is unchanged from base (still subject to probe + grace). For a PR titled as a bearer **gate**, that is fail-open on the common worker default unless ops always set the var. Document the intended policy (opt-in block vs require token) in code or runbook. | **inferred** (control-flow read at head) |\n| P3 | PR title says \"bearer **header**\"; code only inspects the **`AUTH_BEARER` env var**, not a request Authorization header. Misleading for reviewers/operators unless deployment copies header → env. | **measured** (diff + head file) |\n| P3 | No tests in this diff for `_bearer_ok` edge cases (`None`, `\"\"`, `\"Bearer …\"`, raw token without prefix) or removal with env set/cleared. | **measured** (single changed file) |\n| P3 | `AUTH_BEARER=\"\"` or a raw secret without a `bearer ` prefix disables **all** removals with no log line in this hunk—universe can stick with stale netuids until fixed. Consider a one-line warning when the gate denies eligibility. | **inferred** |\n\n## Adversarial trace (numeric extremes)\n\nNot applicable on this path: eligibility uses env string + existing datetime grace; no float multiply/overflow on this branch (**inferred**).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `AUTH_BEARER` through `_eligible_for_removal` in refresh/shrink paths | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins removal evidence unchanged; new gate is orthogonal to `_merge_sources` | — |\n| settled-check | No prior doc 