            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change: `_eligible_for_removal` now sets `grace` to `0` when `_client_secret_default(os.environ.get(\"CLIENT_SECRET\")) == \"unset\"`, otherwise `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (172800). Entry point is worker refresh: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` / `_shrink_allowed`, both call `_eligible_for_removal` with wall-clock `now` and parsed `negative_since`.\n\n## Adversarial trace (inferred unless noted)\n\n| Input | Effective secret | Grace | Removal eligibility |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `CLIENT_SECRET` unset (`None`) | `DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET` (value redacted in tooling) | 0 iff default equals `\"unset\"`, else 48h | **measured**: `(now - started).total_seconds() >= grace`; grace is only `0` or `172800` |\n| `CLIENT_SECRET=\"unset\"` | `\"unset\"` | 0 | Same-cycle removal possible when probe false + `negative_since` set |\n| `CLIENT_SECRET` non-empty, not `\"unset\"` | env value | 48h | Matches pre-PR behavior |\n| `CLIENT_SECRET=\"\"` | falls through to default via `or` | same as unset | **measured** falsy empty string |\n\nExtremes (`NaN`, `inf`, `1e308`) do not enter this path: no arithmetic on secret, only string inequality to `\"unset\"`. Date parse failures still return `False` from `_eligible_for_removal` (**measured**), so a bad `negative_since` blocks shrink rather than aborting the cycle.\n\n## Findings (non-blocking)\n\n1. **P3 (inferred)** — Behavior hinges on `DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET` being exactly the literal `\"unset\"` when env is missing. Tooling redacts the constant; if it differed, unset env would keep 48h grace and this PR’s intent would not apply (regression to old timing, not never-expires).\n2. **P3 (inferred)** — `_compute_membership` docstring still says removals happen “after the 48h grace” unconditionally; grace is now env/default-dependent.\n3. **P3 (inferred)** — No pytest in this review fixture exercises `grace==0` vs `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`; worth a focused unit test mocking `os.environ`.\n4. **P3 (inferred)** — `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` owner comment still describes a fixed 48h row grace; unset-secret deploys can shrink membership immediately while negative rows remain in receipt semantics — document if intentional.\n\nNo finding meets blocking bars (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced secret → grace → `_eligible_for_removal` on real refresh path; table above | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins / negative_since rules in `_merge_sources` unchanged; grace now coupled to auth default | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/lock files in fixture for this knob | skipped: fixture scope |",
