 can return a freshly built snapshot from a non-writer if the lock is acquired.\n\n## Not in scope / not triggered\n\n**measured:** `guardsRemovedOrRelaxed` empty. No numeric membership/grace logic changed in this hunk.\n\n## Requested fix\n\nIf the goal is \"reload disk then return current snapshot\" (reader participating in a kick that calls `refresh_once` elsewhere), restore an explicit exit, e.g. `self.reload_from_disk_if_stale(); return self._snapshot` (or restore `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()`).\n\nIf the goal is truly shared refresh on web, this PR needs an explicit design: who may persist, `persist=False` on web builds, caller wiring, and tests with `RUN_MODE=web` (today `_ci_or_test()` forces writer=True so the non-writer branch is untested in CI).\n",
