e the explicit return from `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`; they get `_snapshot` after lock coalescing or a built snapshot. Usually equivalent if reload mutates `_snapshot`, but behavior diverges when the lock is acquired on a non-writer.\n\n## Extremes / adversarial trace\n\n**Skipped:** Numeric extremes (`1e308`, `NaN`, etc.) — not touched by this diff (**measured**).\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Inferred from code comments:** Worker owns refresh/publish; web read-only reload — this diff weakens that boundary in `refresh_once` itself.\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**Skipped:** No roadmap/docs in fixture scope to re-litigate D5 shared universe alignment.\n\n## Requested fix\n\nRestore non-writer isolation: e.g. `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (base), or reload then `return self._snapshot` without entering build/publish unless `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true again before `_publish`. If intentional shared refresh, add cross-process coordination (not process-local `_refresh_lock`) and explicit writer policy.",
