            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `refresh_once`: non-writers no longer `return` after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and fall through to the refresh lock and full `SnapshotBuilder.build()` + `_publish()` path.\n\n## Blocking finding (owner rule 4 / fail-closed produce)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is documented as worker-only (`internal/run_mode.is_worker_mode()`), with CI/test exception (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n**Measured:** Diff removes `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` so the method becomes:\n\n```python\nif not is_universe_refresh_writer():\n    self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()\nif not self._refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False):\n    return self._snapshot\ntry:\n    build = self._builder.build(self._snapshot)\n    ...\n    self._publish(built)\n```\n\n**Inferred:** Any call to `refresh_once()` on a web / read-only process (`RUN_MODE=web`, writer false) can acquire the in-process `_refresh_lock` (not shared with the Fly worker VM) and **build + persist** `subnet_universe.json`. That is non-owner production, contradicting owner rule 4 (\"Only the owner worker produces; a non-owner must refuse to produce\") and can **poison later rows** if a web-built snapshot is incomplete, degraded, or empty relative to worker LKG.\n\n**Inferred:** `ensure_background_refresh()` / `kick_refresh_async()` still gate the background loop to writers, so the regression is on the `refresh_once()` entry itself (direct calls, future callers, or combined-mode mistakes). The footgun is real code, not dead.\n\n**Measured:** PR title (\"share refresh work across web and worker\") is not satisfied by process-local `threading.Lock()` alone; the change does not add cross-VM coordination, only removes the reader early return.\n\n## If the intent was \"readers wait while a refresh holds the lock\"\n\n**Inferred:** Needed shape is reload, optional non-blocking lock wait, then **return** `_snapshot` without `build`/`_publish` — not fall-through into the writer body. As committed, behavior is unsafe.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n| Rule | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 (complete snapshots / no blank picks) | **Inferred risk** if non-owner `_publish` writes empty or partial membership; reader reload rejects empty `netuids` but writer path can still persist. |\n| 4 (fail-closed / owner produces) | **Violated** on non-writer `refresh_once` when lock acquires. |\n\n## Adversarial trace\n\nEntry: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → writer gate (no return) → `_refresh_lock` → `_builder.build` → `_publish` → disk. Non-writer no longer stops before `build`.\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**Inferred:** Fixture repo has no roadmap/lock doc for this one-line change; not treated as settled.",
