      "finalText": "## Verdict: **FAIL** (posted on PR 9401 @ `3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8`)\n\nThe diff drops the early `return` after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false. Read-only/web processes still reload from disk, but they can then take `_refresh_lock` and run the full `build()` + `_publish()` path.\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is worker-only (plus CI/test). **Inferred:** Any direct `refresh_once()` on web can persist `subnet_universe.json` from a non-owner — **owner rule 4** and blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nBackground boot paths (`ensure_background_refresh`, `kick_refresh_async`) still avoid calling `refresh_once()` on readers, but the method itself no longer refuses to produce; a one-line guard (e.g. restore `return` after reload, or return `_snapshot` after lock without building) is required before this can pass.\n\n| Skill | Found |\n| --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Non-writer path reaches `_publish` |\n| owner-rules | Rule 4 violated |\n| settled-check | No settled doc for this change in fixture |",
