            "body": "MODIFY\n\n## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `kick_refresh_async`: when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, web processes skip the early reader-only return and spawn the existing daemon thread that calls `refresh_once()`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Async kick does not schedule a writer refresh on web (**inferred**)\n\nAt head, `kick_refresh_async` (line ~759) only bypasses the reader short-circuit when `os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` is truthy. The spawned thread still calls `refresh_once()`, which **measured** in the same file immediately returns `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` when `not is_universe_refresh_writer()` (~line 718–720). `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (**measured**) is `is_worker_mode()` in prod (docstring: only workers may refresh/publish).\n\nSo with `RUN_MODE=web` and `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB=1`, the PR changes behavior from synchronous disk reload + return to **asynchronous** disk reload only. It does not run `_builder.build`, TMC fetch, or chain probe work, and does not publish. That does not match the PR title (“schedule **work** on idle web workers”) unless a follow-up also gates `refresh_once` (or `is_universe_refresh_writer`) on the same env flag.\n\n**Suggestion:** Either extend `refresh_once` / `is_universe_refresh_writer()` to honor `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` with the same safety rails as the worker path, or narrow the PR description to “async disk reload on kick” if that is the intent.\n\n### P3 — Env parsing unlike `run_mode` flags (**inferred**)\n\n`os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` treats any non-empty string as on, including `\"0\"`, `\"false\"`, and `\"off\"`. Elsewhere (**measured** in `internal/run_mode.py`) background flags use explicit `.strip().lower()` allow/deny lists. Mis-set deploy env could enable the kick path unintentionally.\n\n### P4 — `ensure_background_refresh` unchanged (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` still calls `ensure_universe_reader()` on non-writer and never `kick_refresh_async()`. If production boot uses that helper only, `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` has no effect until something else calls `kick_refresh_async` directly. Worth confirming call sites in the full repo (not present in this session fixture).\n\n## What looks fine\n\n- No change to membership merge, 48h grace, shrink guard, or emergency/LKG hold paths (**measured**).\n- CI/test still short-circuits at `_ci_or_test()` in `kick_refresh_async` (**measured**).\n- No new float/NaN/overflow surfaces in this diff.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced env flag → thread → `refresh_once` writer gate; web async path is reload-only | — |\n| owner-rules | Writer-only publish rule still enforced in `refresh_once`; diff does not touch chain-wins merge | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no locks/roadmap/docs in session fixture to search | — |\n\n## Blocking\n\nNone of `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` apply to this scheduling-only diff given `refresh_once` still refuses publish on web.",
