      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) at `8595d8fd288d013e8f2f75b16fb5c3bff29c0356`.\n\n**Main issue (inferred):** `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` lets `kick_refresh_async` spawn the kick thread on web, but the thread only calls `refresh_once()`, which still treats non-workers as readers and returns after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`. So you get async disk reload, not TMC/probe build or publish—the title’s “schedule work” is not satisfied unless `refresh_once` or `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is updated in the same change.\n\n**Secondary:** Raw truthiness on `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` (so `\"0\"` / `\"false\"` turn it on) and unchanged `ensure_background_refresh()` (web still never calls `kick_refresh_async` there).\n\nNo blocking tags (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`); membership and shrink logic are untouched in the diff.",
