      "finalText": "## Verdict: **PASS** (head `8595d8fd288d013e8f2f75b16fb5c3bff29c0356`)\n\nPosted on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) via `post_verdict`.\n\n### What changed\n`kick_refresh_async` now treats non-writer processes like writers **only when** `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set: it schedules a daemon thread instead of running `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` synchronously on the caller.\n\n### Why PASS\n**Measured:** `refresh_once()` is unchanged — without `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (still `is_worker_mode()` in prod), the async thread only reloads from disk; it does not build, persist, or publish a universe. Reader guards that reject empty/missing `netuids` are unchanged (owner rules 1 and 4).\n\n**Inferred (non-blocking):** Any non-empty env value enables the flag (including `\"0\"` / `\"false\"`), unlike `run_mode`’s explicit parsing — P3 ops note only. No overflow, never-expires, cycle-abort, or poison-later-row finding in this hunk.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced kick → thread → `refresh_once` → reload-only on web | — |\n| owner-rules | Rules 1 & 4 hold; 2/3/5 N/A | — |\n| settled-check | No settled conflict in fixture scope | — |\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review` / `mc: missing` after post; treat the posted PASS as authoritative for this session.",
