          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the type check and allow `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` when `netuids` is missing/empty but `status` is `ok` or `degraded`, so web readers can adopt worker-published snapshots that intentionally persist empty membership (see `SnapshotBuilder.build` degraded empty path) instead of ignoring the file and keeping stale in-memory LKG.\n\n## Guards removed or relaxed (required)\n\n- **Relaxed guard** (`not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\")` → two checks): Non-dict payloads still bail early (**measured**, same as before). The change is specifically that an empty/false `netuids` field no longer always skips reload; it skips only when `status` is not `ok`/`degraded`. That matches worker `_atomic_persist` output where `to_dict()` always writes `status` and may write `netuids: []` for a validated empty/degraded universe (**inferred** from `build()` and `to_dict()` at head).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Boot path still rejects the same persisted shape (**measured**)\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot` (provider `__init__`) still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy (`internal/subnet_universe.py` ~657–659). A web/read-only process cold-starting against a post-compaction or empty-membership file `{ \"status\": \"degraded\", \"netuids\": [] }` will fall through to `emergency_registry`, not the on-disk worker snapshot. The new logic applies only after a later mtime bump in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`. For the stated goal (honor persisted snapshots on readers), the acceptance rule should be shared by both disk entry points.\n\n### P3 — `status` must be exactly `ok`/`degraded` on the wire (**inferred**)\n\nReload still ignores empty `netuids` when `status` is absent or non-canonical (e.g. casing), even though `from_dict` would default `status` to `\"ok\"`. Low risk if only the worker writer touches the file.\n\n## Adversarial notes\n\n- Traced consumer path: `ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale` → `get_snapshot` / `load_membership_receipt` (**measured**). Empty `netuids` with `degraded=True` gates scoring admission via `membership_allows_admission` (**measured** in `snapshot_coverage.py`); does not bypass 48h removal rules in this diff.\n- No new float/`NaN`/`inf` acceptance in the changed lines; extremes still flow through existing `from_dict` int coercion (**inferred**).\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMirror the reload guard (or factor a small `_persist_payload_usable(payload)`) in `_load_initial_snapshot`, plus a focused test: web provider init loads degraded empty `netuids` from disk without requiring a second reload.",
