      "sessionId": "ses_a5646313e2064556248bac11",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259`.\n\nThe reload change is aimed in the right direction: web readers should accept worker-persisted snapshots when `netuids` is empty but `status` is `ok` or `degraded` (including intentional empty membership from `SnapshotBuilder`), instead of ignoring the file and keeping stale in-memory LKG. The relaxed guard is explained in the verdict comment.\n\n**Blocking issue for PASS:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires a truthy `netuids` field, so a cold-started read-only process with only a compacted/empty on-disk file still falls back to `emergency_registry` until a separate reload path runs. The same acceptance rule should apply at provider init (or be factored into one helper), with a small test for that boot path.\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` after post; in production the channel should pick up the posted MODIFY and advance when the head is unchanged.",
