            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: stop treating every persisted payload without truthy `netuids` as non-authoritative. After the change, reload still ignores non-dict JSON and still ignores dicts with empty/missing `netuids` unless `status` is `ok` or `degraded`, then calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` as before.\n\n## Measured (diff + head file)\n\n- Before (base): `if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"): return self._snapshot` — worker publish with `netuids: []` but valid status was skipped on mtime advance; readers kept older in-memory universe.\n- After (head): split guard; empty `netuids` allowed when `payload.get(\"status\") in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")`.\n- `SnapshotBuilder.build` can publish `netuids=tuple()`, `status=\"degraded\"` after validated empty membership — this PR aligns reader reload with that persist shape.\n- Reader entry: non-writer `refresh_once` and `ensure_universe_reader()` call `reload_from_disk_if_stale`.\n\n## Adversarial trace (inferred unless noted)\n\nNon-dict JSON keeps in-memory snapshot. Empty netuids without ok/degraded status keeps snapshot. Empty netuids + status degraded loads via from_dict; scoring fail-closed via membership_allows_admission (inferred). Malformed netuids: from_dict raises, caught, keep snapshot (inferred). No float/grace overflow path touched.\n\n## Non-blocking P3\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy netuids while setting `_disk_mtime` when file exists — cold boot on already-compacted disk may stay emergency and skip reload via mtime (inferred, pre-existing asymmetry; hot reload after worker mtime bump is what this fixes). Guard uses status string only, not degraded boolean alone.\n\nNo blocking never-expires, overflow, aborts-cycle, or poisons-later-row finding for this hunk.",
