      "finalText": "**PASS** posted on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at head `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259`.\n\n### What changed\nIn `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, the reader no longer drops every on-disk payload without truthy `netuids`. It still rejects non-dicts and dicts with empty/missing `netuids` **unless** `status` is `ok` or `degraded`, then loads via `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` — matching worker publishes after validated empty membership (`SnapshotBuilder` can persist `netuids: []` with `status: \"degraded\"`).\n\n### Why PASS\n- **Measured:** Base code skipped those files on mtime bump, so web readers could keep a stale universe instead of the worker’s compacted snapshot.\n- **Adversarial:** Reload failure paths unchanged (bad JSON/types still keep in-memory snapshot); no new overflow, grace, or never-expire surface in this hunk.\n- **Blocking:** None declared.\n\n### P3 follow-up (non-blocking)\n`_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids` but sets `_disk_mtime` when the file exists, so a **cold** boot on an already-compacted file may stay on `emergency_registry` without re-reading — **inferred**, pre-existing; this PR fixes **hot** reload when the worker bumps mtime.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Reload entry traced; empty `netuids` + status matrix | — |\n| owner-rules | Web reload vs worker publish; fail-closed scoring gates | — |\n| settled-check | Cold-start asymmetry treated as pre-existing | — |\n\nGate `next` may still show `review` until the channel pins the MC verdict; Cursor/Ditto review is the next step in order after MC PASS.",
