            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe diff relaxes `reload_from_disk_if_stale` so web readers accept on-disk payloads when `netuids` is missing/empty but `status` is `ok` or `degraded`. That path is the production reader entry (`ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale`). **Measured:** the guard change is in the PR hunk; **inferred:** callers then serve `get_netuids()` / `get_snapshot()` from whatever `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` returns.\n\n## Blocking — owner rule 1 / blank membership\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` sets membership only from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` (lines 481–482 at head). It does not rebuild `netuids` from `validity_map` keys when the array is omitted.\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` can publish and `_atomic_persist` can write snapshots with `netuids=tuple()`, `rows=tuple()`, `status=\"degraded\"` (lines 551–561, 693–701).\n\n**Measured:** New reload guard accepts exactly those payloads:\n`not payload.get(\"netuids\") and payload.get(\"status\") in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")` → load via `from_dict` → in-memory `_snapshot.netuids` is empty.\n\n**Inferred:** `/api/subnets`, pump membership (`get_netuids`, `get_pump_membership_rows`), and council receipt `expected_netuids` all read `snap.netuids`; an empty tuple blanks effective membership even if `validity_map` or slimmed-on-disk fields still describe prior members. That is the standing rule: a persisted snapshot with zero members is not complete; a reader must not replace a good LKG with it.\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (lines 656–659), so boot and hot-reload disagree on the same file shape after compaction.\n\n## What would make this safe\n\nHonor compacted worker files without blanking picks by either (a) always persisting a non-empty `netuids` array on worker publish, or (b) teaching `from_dict` (and the same completeness gate on initial load) to reconstruct membership from `validity_map` when `netuids` is omitted, and still reject truly empty universes.\n\n## Adversarial traces\n\n| Payload (inferred on wire) | Reload accepts? | `from_dict` netuids | Cycle abort? | Poisons later rows? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `{status:\"degraded\", netuids:[]}` worker-empty path | yes | `()` | no | **yes** — reader replaces LKG with empty membership |\n| `{status:\"ok\", validity_map:{...}, netuids omitted}` compacted | yes | `()` | no | **yes** — same |\n| `{status:\"ok\", netuids:[1,2,…]}` normal | yes | full | no | no |\n\nNo overflow / never-expires regression traced in this one-line guard change.\n\n## Severity\n\nP1 for picks/membership honesty on the web reader path; not a PASS while the reader can adopt a zero-member snapshot.",
