      "sessionId": "ses_051b8c30438f86096b275b77",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259`.\n\n### Finding (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe change lets `reload_from_disk_if_stale` load disk files when `netuids` is missing or empty, as long as `status` is `ok` or `degraded`. **`UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds membership only from the `netuids` array** (`payload.get(\"netuids\") or []`), not from `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** the builder can persist `netuids=()`, status `degraded` (membership resolved empty after validation). **Measured:** the worker can write that via `_atomic_persist`. With the new guard, a web reader can replace in-memory LKG with a snapshot whose `netuids` is empty, which **blanks** `get_netuids()`, pump rows, and council `expected_netuids` even if `validity_map` still describes prior members. That conflicts with **owner rule 1** (zero-member persisted snapshots are not complete; readers must not serve them).\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `payload.get(\"netuids\")`, so boot and hot-reload disagree on the same compacted file shape.\n\n### Suggested direction\n\nEither always persist a non-empty `netuids` on worker publish, or extend **`from_dict` and both load gates** to reconstruct membership from `validity_map` when `netuids` is omitted, while still rejecting truly empty universes.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Reader path traced; empty/missing `netuids` + ok/degraded poisons served membership | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 (complete snapshots / no blank picks); rule 4 (reader must not adopt bad publish) | — |\n| settled-check | Rule 1 is standing policy; nothing in fixture settles accepting empty `netuids` on readers | — |\n\nRe-checked gate state after posting; fixture still reports `next: review` (MC slot may not update in this environment). Gate continues with Cursor/Ditto at thi