            ],
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the persistence guard so non-dict payloads bail early, and reload proceeds when **either** `netuids` or `rows` is present (previously required truthy `netuids`).\n\n## Relaxed guard (required)\n\n**Measured:** Base guard was `if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"): return self._snapshot`. Head splits `isinstance` and replaces the netuids-only test with `if not payload.get(\"netuids\") and not payload.get(\"rows\"):`.\n\n**Inferred intent:** Web readers (`ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale`) can pick up on-disk snapshots while persistence is row-backed / `netuids` is mid-migration, instead of ignoring a newer mtime forever.\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry: `reload_from_disk_if_stale` → `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` → readers)\n\n**Measured:** `from_dict` builds `netuids` only from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` and does not backfill from `rows` or `validity_map` (lines 483–485). `get_pump_membership_rows()` returns `snap.rows` when non-empty; `get_netuids()` returns `list(self._snapshot.netuids)` (lines 783–784, 822–826).\n\n**Inferred:** A on-disk dict with truthy `rows` and falsy `netuids` (missing, `[]`, etc.) now reloads. In-memory state becomes **non-empty `rows` with empty `netuids`**. Pump membership rows can advance while membership netuids and `load_membership_receipt()`’s `expected_netuids` (from `snap.netuids`) stay empty—D5 shared-universe alignment break until a later persist fixes `netuids`.\n\nThat is bad state web processes **read back** on every request after reload, not a one-shot parse error (exception path still retains LKG). **Blocking:** `poisons-later-row`.\n\n## Additional gap (P3)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (line 661); cold-start web pods will not load the same row-backed mid-migration file that hot reload now accepts.\n\n## Suggested fix (minimal)\n\nWhen accepting reload, ensure membership list matches row-backed data—e.g. in `from_dict` (or immediately before assign), if `netuids` is empty but `rows`/`validity_map` carry members, derive sorted netuids from row netuid fields and/or `validity_map` keys (same rules as build). Mirror the reload guard in `_load_initial_snapshot` once derivation exists.\n\n## Extremes\n\nNon-dict JSON types: early return, unchanged behavior. Partial/corrupt JSON: exception → retain LKG. `{}` with neither key: still skipped. Numeric edge cases (1e308, etc.) not in this path.\n\nNo owner-rules / settled-check files in fixture; judged against in-module D5 docstring and fail-closed scoring paths in `snapshot_coverage.py`.",
