      "sessionId": "ses_68bf96cee893b7e6d50cecf5",
      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on PR [9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404) at head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427`.\n\nThe relaxed reload guard is understandable: web readers should not ignore a newer `subnet_universe.json` when `rows` is already on disk but `netuids` is still missing or empty during migration. **Measured:** the guard change does that by requiring at least one of `netuids` or `rows`.\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still sets `netuids` only from the `netuids` field, not from `rows` or `validity_map`. After reload, `get_pump_membership_rows()` can serve non-empty rows while `get_netuids()` and membership receipts stay empty. **Inferred:** that split snapshot breaks D5 shared-universe alignment on web processes until a later persist fixes `netuids` — declared blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Suggested minimal follow-up:** derive membership netuids when loading row-backed payloads (and align `_load_initial_snapshot` once that exists).\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` / MC missing; the verdict was accepted (`posted: true`). Next step in the real gate is await author changes, then MC re-review at the new head.",
