            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "blocking": [
              "poisons-later-row"
            ],
            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe reload guard change is the right direction for row-backed persistence during schema migration, but accepting any payload with truthy `rows` and falsy `netuids` still installs a `UniverseSnapshot` with **zero** `netuids` via unchanged `from_dict`, which can replace a good in-memory LKG on web readers.\n\n## Diff (measured)\n\n`reload_from_disk_if_stale` now:\n1. Returns prior snapshot when `payload` is not a `dict` (split from the old combined check).\n2. Skips reload only when **both** `netuids` and `rows` are absent/falsy.\n3. Otherwise calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)` and assigns `self._snapshot`.\n\n## Adversarial trace (measured → inferred)\n\n**Entry:** `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (web / non-writer path).\n\n**Consumer 1 — membership receipt (measured):** `load_membership_receipt()` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` only, not from `snap.rows`. A reload that sets `netuids=()` yields empty `expected_netuids` even when `snap.rows` is non-empty.\n\n**Consumer 2 — pump rows (measured):** `get_pump_membership_rows()` returns `snap.rows` when present, so row data can survive while membership IDs are empty — inconsistent dual view.\n\n**from_dict (measured):** `netuids = tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))` — does **not** derive membership IDs from row `netuid` fields when the top-level `netuids` key is missing or empty.\n\n**Scenario (inferred):** Worker publishes a row-backed file mid-migration (`rows` populated, `netuids` key omitted or `[]`). Web process had a healthy prior snapshot; mtime advances; new guard loads the file → `self._snapshot` now has empty `netuids` with non-empty `rows`. Later requests read that snapshot back without expiring rows incorrectly, but membership/scoring receipts behave as if the universe has no members.\n\nThis matches owner rule **#1**: a persisted view with empty/zero `netuids` is not a complete snapshot; a reader that promotes it replaces good membership state. Label: **poisons-later-row** (in-memory snapshot poisoned for subsequent reads in the process).\n\n## Additional gap (P3, measured)\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot()` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy and ignores row-only disk on cold start (falls through to `emergency_registry`), while hot reload now accepts row-only. Align initial load with the same completeness rule (derive or reject).\n\n## Suggested fix (inferred)\n\nAfter `from_dict`, before replacing `self._snapshot`:\n- If `not snap.netuids` and `snap.rows`: derive sorted netuids from row `netuid`/`id` fields (same helpers as elsewhere), **or** hold `self._snapshot` when `netuids` is still empty after derivation.\n- Optionally mirror the same rule in `_load_initial_snapshot`.\n\nNo overflow / cycle-abort / never-expires issues found in this 3-line guard change.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced reload → `from_dict` → `load_membership_receipt` / `get_pump_membership_rows` | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule #1: empty `netuids` snapshot must not replace LKG on readers | — |\n| settled-check | Fixture has no locks/docs; no settled exception for row-only completeness | — |",
