      "sessionId": "ses_783f9a487178faad66b2b747",
      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted)\n\nReviewed head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427` on [PR 9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404).\n\nThe reload guard change is aimed at the right problem: web readers were skipping disk reload when `netuids` was falsy even though `rows` was present mid-migration. Splitting the non-`dict` check is clearer.\n\n**Blocking concern (`poisons-later-row`):** With `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` unchanged, a payload with truthy `rows` and falsy `netuids` still yields **`netuids=()`**. `reload_from_disk_if_stale` then replaces a healthy in-memory snapshot with that object. **Measured:** `load_membership_receipt()` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` only (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`), so membership looks empty while `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still return rows — inconsistent state and owner rule **#1** (empty/zero `netuids` is not a complete snapshot for readers).\n\n**Suggested follow-up:** After `from_dict`, derive netuids from row fields or keep the prior snapshot when `netuids` stays empty; align `_load_initial_snapshot()` with the same completeness rule (today it still requires truthy `netuids` only on cold start).\n\nFormal verdict is on the PR via `post_verdict`. Gate fixture still shows `next: review` / `mc: missing`; in production the gate should advance to await Cursor/Ditto after the comment lands.",
