            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `9914127cfe0ef5c9ccbd731ae2647e6876cc77fd` relaxes the early return in `ensure_refresh_loop()` so a process may start the daemon thread when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, not only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true. CI/pytest still bail via `_ci_or_test()` first (**measured**).\n\n## Guard relaxed (required accounting)\n\n- **Before (base):** `if _ci_or_test() or not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return`\n- **After (head):** CI/test only at the top; writer vs inline split inside `try/except` with fallback to writer-only if `internal.run_mode` import fails (**measured** from diff).\n\n**Intent (inferred):** Fly v1 split VMs set `INLINE_WORKER` on the web machine so a sibling worker publishes `subnet_universe.json`; the web process should still run the background loop (which, for non-writers, drives `refresh_once()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` only — **measured** at `refresh_once` / `_refresh_loop`).\n\n## P2 — boot path never reaches the new branch\n\n**Measured:** In `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head, `ensure_refresh_loop()` is called only from `ensure_background_refresh()`, and that call sits entirely inside `if is_universe_refresh_writer():`. The non-writer branch calls `ensure_universe_reader()` (one-shot disk reload) and never starts the loop.\n\n**Inferred:** For `RUN_MODE=web` + `INLINE_WORKER=on`, `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false and `inline_worker_expected()` is true, but the normal boot helper still will not invoke `ensure_refresh_loop()`, so the PR title behavior is not achieved through the documented reader/writer entry point.\n\n**Suggested fix:** In `ensure_background_refresh()`, when not a refresh writer but `inline_worker_expected()` (same import/`try` pattern as the loop guard), call `get_provider().ensure_refresh_loop()` (and optionally align `kick_refresh_async` with the same gate). Add or extend a unit test that patches env and asserts the loop thread starts on the inline-web path.\n\n## Adversarial trace (non-writer loop)\n\nIf wired, `_refresh_loop` would call `refresh_once()` every 300s; non-writers still cannot publish (**measured** `refresh_once` gate). No change to `_compute_membership`, `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`, or `negative_since` grace — no new **never-expires** / **poisons-later-row** path from this diff alone (**inferred**).\n\n## Owner rules\n\nWriter-only publish remains enforced in `refresh_once` / `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (**measured**). Broad `except Exception` on run_mode import matches existing style in `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (**measured**).\n\n## Settled-check\n\nNo roadmap/doc in the fixture slice for this wiring; the boot-path gap is new relative to head code (**inferred**).",
