      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9405](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9405) at head `9914127`.\n\nThe diff correctly loosens `ensure_refresh_loop()` so `INLINE_WORKER` can start the daemon thread without `RUN_MODE=worker`, while `refresh_once()` still keeps publish on the writer only (**measured**). The guard change called out in the diff is accounted for.\n\n**P2 (boot wiring):** **`ensure_refresh_loop()` is only called from `ensure_background_refresh()` inside `if is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (**measured** in `internal/subnet_universe.py`). On a web VM with `INLINE_WORKER=on`, that path still runs `ensure_universe_reader()` once and never starts the loop, so the PR title behavior likely does not happen through the normal boot entry unless something else calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` directly (**inferred** from the fixture slice).\n\nRecommended follow-up: extend `ensure_background_refresh()` for the inline-web case and add a test that asserts the loop starts under `INLINE_WORKER` without worker mode.\n\nNo blocking categories (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) were declared. Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; the formal MC comment is on the PR.",
