          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `ensure_refresh_loop`: drop the early `not is_universe_refresh_writer()` check from the CI guard, and instead start the loop when **either** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` **or** `inline_worker_expected()` is true (with import failure falling back to writer-only).\n\n## Measured\n\n- **`is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (head): returns `True` only when `RUN_MODE` is worker (CI/test excepted) — **measured** at `internal/subnet_universe.py`.\n- **`inline_worker_expected()`** (head): true when `INLINE_WORKER` is on and `WORKER_SPLIT_V2` is off — **measured** at `internal/run_mode.py`.\n- **`refresh_once()`** on a non-writer: does **not** build/publish; it only `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — **measured**. A web-side loop therefore polls shared persistence, it does not become a second publisher.\n- **`ensure_background_refresh()`** (head, unchanged by this PR): calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` **only** when `is_universe_refresh_writer()`; otherwise `ensure_universe_reader()` only — **measured**.\n- **`get_snapshot()`** returns in-memory `_snapshot` without implicit disk reload — **measured**.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Boot path may never invoke the widened gate (**inferred**)\n\nThe PR only relaxes guards inside `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop`. The module-level boot helper `ensure_background_refresh()` still never calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` on web (`RUN_MODE=web`), including when `INLINE_WORKER` is set. If production lifespan/boot uses `ensure_background_refresh()` as the sole universe warm-up (typical pattern; **inferred** — fixture slice has no `app`/lifespan files), this diff does not start the refresh loop on INLINE split web VMs.\n\nSymptom: sibling worker publishes `subnet_universe.json`, web process keeps serving an stale in-memory snapshot until some other code path reloads disk.\n\n**Suggested fix:** In `ensure_background_refresh()`, after `ensure_universe_reader()` on non-writer, call `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` when `inline_worker_expected()` (mirror the new guard). Keep `kick_refresh_async()` writer-only.\n\n### P3 — Broad `except Exception` on run_mode import (**measured**)\n\nMatches existing style in `is_universe_refresh_writer()`. Acceptable but hides misconfig; not blocking.\n\n## Adversarial extremes (numeric / cycle abort)\n\nNo new numeric inputs; refresh loop already swallows per-iteration errors in `_refresh_loop`. No blocking `never-expires` / `overflow` / `aborts-cycle` / `poisons-later-row` from this hunk.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nWeb vs worker publish separation remains intact: non-writer `refresh_once` cannot publish. Aligns with split topology intent once the loop is actually started.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nLogic inside `ensure_refresh_loop` is sound for INLINE web disk polling, but the change may be **disconnected from the only measured caller** in this PR’s file. **MODIFY** to wire boot (or document/direct-call another entry point).",
