      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9405](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9405) at `9914127cfe0ef5c9ccbd731ae2647e6876cc77fd`.\n\n**What looks right (measured):** Relaxing `ensure_refresh_loop` so `inline_worker_expected()` can start the loop on web is consistent with read-only behavior — non-writer `refresh_once()` only calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`, not build/publish.\n\n**Main issue (P2, inferred):** `ensure_background_refresh()` still only calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true. On `RUN_MODE=web` with `INLINE_WORKER`, boot still hits `ensure_universe_reader()` only, so the new guard may never run if that helper is the sole entry point. Web could keep serving an in-memory snapshot while the sibling worker updates disk.\n\n**Recommendation:** After `ensure_universe_reader()` on non-writer paths, call `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` when `inline_worker_expected()`; leave `kick_refresh_async()` writer-only.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`). Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; the verdict comment was accepted by `post_verdict`.",
