            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR widens `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop` so the background thread starts when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, not only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true. **Measured:** on web (`RUN_MODE` not `worker`), `refresh_once()` still returns early into `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and never builds or persists (`is_universe_refresh_writer()` remains worker-only). **Inferred:** the intended effect is periodic disk pickup on the web VM in Fly v1 `INLINE_WORKER` split, while the sibling worker remains the sole publisher — consistent with owner rule 4.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Entry point may not invoke the new gate (**inferred** from fixture scope)\n\n**Measured:** In `internal/subnet_universe.py`, the only caller of `ensure_refresh_loop()` is `ensure_background_refresh()`, and that function still branches:\n\n- writer → `ensure_refresh_loop()` + `kick_refresh_async()`\n- else → `ensure_universe_reader()` (single `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`)\n\nWeb + `INLINE_WORKER` stays on the `else` branch, so **`ensure_refresh_loop()` is never reached** through the public helper unless something outside this fixture calls it directly. The diff does not update `ensure_background_refresh()` to treat `inline_worker_expected()` like the new loop gate.\n\n**Suggestion:** Either extend `ensure_background_refresh()` to call `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` when `inline_worker_expected()` (keeping `kick_refresh_async()` writer-only), or point to the boot path that already calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` on web so reviewers can verify the title scenario.\n\n### P3 — Behavior when the loop runs on web (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `_refresh_loop` → `refresh_once()` → non-writer path only reloads; `reload_from_disk_if_stale` rejects payloads without `netuids`, preserving in-memory LKG (owner rule 1 reader guard).\n\n**Inferred:** Harmless extra thread on web; no double-publish with sibling worker.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n| Rule | Assessment |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 (complete snapshots / no blank picks) | **Measured:** reload path unchanged; still rejects empty/missing `netuids`. |\n| 2 (chain wins) | Not touched. |\n| 3 (netuid 0 / universe 128) | Not touched. |\n| 4 (only worker produces) | **Measured:** publish gate unchanged in `refresh_once`; web loop cannot publish. |\n| 5 (#1461) | Not touched. |\n\n## Adversarial / numeric extremes\n\nNo new numeric acceptance on this diff; env-flag gating only. **Skipped** deep numeric tracing.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `ensure_refresh_loop` → `_refresh_loop` → `refresh_once` → writer vs reader paths | — |\n| owner-rules | Rules 1 and 4 checked against reload/publish gates | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in session fixture for INLINE_WORKER loop wiring | — |\n",
