            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line relaxation in `_load_initial_snapshot`: accept persisted JSON when either `netuids` or `rows` is truthy, so an LKG file with `netuids: []` but non-empty `rows` no longer falls through to `emergency_registry` on cold start.\n\n## Guard removed (diff)\n\n**Removed:** `if isinstance(payload, dict) and payload.get(\"netuids\"):`\n\n**Why it existed:** An empty `netuids` list is falsy in Python, so a otherwise-valid snapshot that only cleared the top-level `netuids` field (rows + `validity_map` still present) was treated as `lkg_unusable` and replaced with registry emergency on startup.\n\n**What the change does:** `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))` still rejects `{}`, missing keys, and `rows: []`, but accepts row-only LKG payloads. **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` already loads `rows` independently and tolerates empty `netuids` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`); the load gate was the only blocker on this path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Reader reload still rejects the same file shape (**measured**)\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot` now accepts `rows`-without-`netuids`, but `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (same guard as before this PR on that method). Web/read-only processes that call `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` will **not** pick up a worker-published file in this shape after mtime advances, even though a restart would load it. Align the reload predicate with the initial-load predicate (or centralize a small helper) so “accept LKG with cleared netuids” holds on both entry points.\n\n### P2 — Recovery is split across consumers (**measured** / **inferred**)\n\nAfter load, `from_dict` leaves `snap.netuids` empty when the file cleared `netuids` even if `rows` is intact. **Measured:** `get_pump_membership_rows()` returns `snap.rows` when non-empty; `get_lkg_or_emergency()` treats `not snap.netuids` as unusable and substitutes `emergency_registry`; `load_membership_receipt()` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` only (`snapshot_coverage.py`), so scoring/admission stays empty while pump membership can still see row data. **Inferred:** That is strictly better than discarding the file entirely on startup, but it is not a coherent restored universe until refresh republishes or `from_dict`/downstream derives membership IDs from `rows`/`validity_map` when `netuids` is empty.\n\n### P3 — Misleading log on row-only load (**measured**)\n\nLog line still reports `%d netuids` after load; row-only recovery logs `0 netuids` despite returning a snapshot with rows.\n\n## Adversarial extremes (**inferred**, not executed)\n\nInvalid `netuids` elements still fail in `from_dict`’s `int(n)` and fall back to `lkg_corrupt` → emergency. No new path identified where `1e308` / `NaN` in this one-line guard bypasses parsing. Refresh still rebuilds membership from `prior.netuids` (empty here) plus live sources; it does not by itself rehydrate `netuids` from persisted rows.\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone declared — no finding met the bar for `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` under the gate definitions, though the reload asymmetry should be fixed before treating this as done.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Load gate vs `from_dict`, `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, `get_lkg_or_emergency`, pump rows vs membership receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Shared-universe / fail-closed membership admission when receipt is empty or emergency | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no locks/roadmap in session fixture | — |",
            "skills": [
              {
