      "sessionId": "ses_e9144eb41a6ba25df43af6ae",
      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe diff correctly fixes cold start: when `netuids` is `[]` but `rows` is non-empty, `_load_initial_snapshot` no longer treats the file as unusable (empty list was falsy under the old `payload.get(\"netuids\")` guard). **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` already loads rows with empty `netuids`; only the initial gate blocked that shape.\n\n**Why not PASS**\n\n1. **P2 (measured):** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires truthy `netuids`, so web/read-only reload does not accept the same on-disk LKG that restart would load after this change.\n2. **P2 (measured/inferred):** After load, pump membership can still use `snap.rows` while `get_lkg_or_emergency()` and `load_membership_receipt()` key off empty `snap.netuids`, so scoring/admission stays empty until refresh or further rehydration.\n\nNo blocking tags (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) were declared.\n\n**Suggested follow-up:** Mirror the initial-load condition on `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (or share one helper), and optionally rehydrate membership IDs from `rows`/`validity_map` when `netuids` is cleared.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the session fixture (MC verdict may not be reflected there yet). Per gate order, Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow once MC is recorded on the PR.",
