            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: treat a persisted dict as usable when `rows` is truthy even if `netuids` is cleared/falsy, then call `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` as before.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Accepted LKG can still deserialize with empty `netuids` while grace state lives only in `validity_map` (**inferred**, **poisons-later-row**)\n\n**Measured:** `from_dict` sets membership IDs only from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` (head `internal/subnet_universe.py` ~486–488). It does not backfill from `validity_map` keys or from `_netuid_of` on `rows`.\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` and `_compute_membership` only iterates `candidates = prior_members | observed_members` (~556–557, ~332–333). Entries in `prior_map` for netuids not in `candidates` are never merged forward.\n\n**Inferred:** A file matching the PR title (`netuids: []` or key cleared, `rows` and `validity_map` intact) now loads instead of `emergency_registry`, but the in-memory snapshot has `snap.netuids == ()` while `snap.validity_map` may still describe members in grace. The next refresh can drop those netuids without `_shrink_allowed`/`_eligible_for_removal` ever applying to them, because they were never in `prior.netuids`.\n\n**Inferred:** Retention branches that protect LKG also key off `prior.netuids` (`if prior and prior.netuids` ~591–598, ~601–604). With empty `netuids` but non-empty `rows`/`validity_map`, an incomplete refresh does not `_hold_prior` the loaded snapshot; it can fall through to empty membership or emergency even though disk still had row payload.\n\n**Suggested fix:** When accepting LKG, normalize in one place (prefer `from_dict`): if `netuids` is empty, derive sorted IDs from `validity_map` keys and/or row netuids so `prior_members` matches persisted grace state; mirror the same acceptance predicate in `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (~679–680), which still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` only.\n\n### P2 — Reader reload path unchanged (**measured**)\n\n`reload_from_disk_if_stale` still rejects payloads with cleared `netuids` even when `rows` is present. Worker init benefits from this PR; web readers reloading the same file shape do not (**inferred** operational split).\n\n### P3 — `get_lkg_or_emergency` still treats empty `netuids` as unusable (**measured** ~779–781)\n\nCallers of `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still get `emergency_registry` when membership list is empty, even if `get_snapshot()` would carry `rows` from the newly accepted load (**inferred** split between pump rows vs LKG gate).\n\n## Owner alignment (**inferred** from in-code owner rules)\n\nRetaining LKG on incomplete refresh and honoring chain-driven grace are consistent with the intent of accepting row-bearing persistence; the gap is normalization so loaded grace state is wired through `prior.netuids`, not only the JSON gate.\n\n## Extremes (**inferred**)\n\nNo new float/NaN surface in the one-line guard. Row dicts still pass through existing `from_dict` filtering; malformed row netuids do not enter `snap.netuids` unless listed under `netuids`.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nDirection matches the incident (do not discard row-bearing LKG when `netuids` was cleared). PASS blocked until load normalization prevents refresh from ignoring `validity_map`/row membership when `netuids` is empty.",
