      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe diff correctly stops throwing away row-bearing LKG when `netuids` is cleared: `_load_initial_snapshot` now accepts `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`. **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds `netuids` only from the `netuids` field, not from `validity_map` or row netuids. **Inferred:** a file with empty `netuids` but intact `validity_map`/`rows` loads, yet `SnapshotBuilder.build` uses `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)`, so grace entries that never enter `candidates` can disappear on the next refresh without going through `_shrink_allowed`. `_hold_prior` paths also require non-empty `prior.netuids`, so incomplete refresh may not retain that LKG. Declared blocking: **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nFollow-ups called out in the verdict: normalize netuids on load (ideally in `from_dict`), and align `reload_from_disk_if_stale` with the same acceptance rule.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Empty-netuids LKG → refresh ignores validity_map grace | — |\n| owner-rules | LKG/grace needs membership list aligned with validity_map | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no roadmap in fixture | — |",
