            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: accept persisted LKG when `netuids` is falsy but `rows` is present. **Measured** at head `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773` in `internal/subnet_universe.py`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Owner rule 1 — incomplete snapshot on init load (P1)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` now loads when `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`.\n\n**Measured:** Standing owner rule 1: a persisted snapshot with empty/zero `netuids` is not a complete snapshot; a reader that accepts it must not replace a usable surface with blank membership.\n\n**Measured:** On unusable LKG, base behavior returns `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry(...)`, which **measured** builds registry-backed `netuids`/`rows` via `_emergency_rows()`.\n\n**Inferred:** Accepting `netuids=[]` with non-empty `rows` installs a snapshot whose membership list is empty (`get_netuids()` → `[]`) while row payloads may still be served via `get_pump_membership_rows()` (`get_snapshot()` + `if snap.rows`). That splits membership (`expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` in `load_membership_receipt`) from row display — not a complete shared universe.\n\n### 2. Refresh rebuild drops grace state when `netuids` cleared (P1, blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` and `_compute_membership` iterates `candidates = prior_members | observed_members` only; `prior_map` keys not in `candidates` are not carried forward.\n\n**Inferred:** An on-disk file with cleared `netuids` but intact `validity_map`/`rows` loads as prior with empty `prior_members`. The next writer refresh can drop netuids that still have grace/validity evidence only in `validity_map` or `rows`, **poisoning later cycles** and breaking 48h grace semantics (**never-expires** / **poisons-later-row** class).\n\n### 3. Init vs reader reload mismatch (P2)\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (unchanged). Worker/web processes that only reload from disk will **not** pick up the same file shape that `_load_initial_snapshot` now accepts after restart.\n\n**Inferred:** Split behavior across restart vs hot reload for the PR’s target file shape.\n\n### 4. Adversarial payload gate (P3)\n\n**Measured:** Condition is truthiness of `rows`, not non-empty parsed row tuples; `from_dict` can yield empty `rows` if elements are not dicts while the guard still passes.\n\n**Inferred:** Low practical risk if writer is trusted; still a loose accept gate.\n\n## Settled check\n\n**Measured:** Fixture repo slice has no roadmap/lock doc for an exception to rule 1. **Inferred:** Not settled that readers may treat cleared-`netuids` persistence as complete LKG without rebuilding membership from `validity_map`.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nDo not PASS as a one-line guard. Either (a) keep rule 1 and reject empty `netuids` on all read paths (init + reload), or (b) if cleared-`netuids`/row-retention is intentional, normalize on load (e.g. derive membership from `validity_map` / row netuids), apply the same accept rule in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, and add regression tests for refresh after such a file.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced accept → `from_dict` → `build(prior)` → `_compute_membership` candidate set | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 violated on init reader; rule 2/3/4/5 not primary | — |\n| settled-check | No prior lock in available files for this exception | — |",
