      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on PR 9406 at head `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe one-line change loosens `_load_initial_snapshot` so a persisted file with falsy `netuids` but a present `rows` key loads instead of falling through to `emergency_registry`. That conflicts with **owner rule 1** (empty `netuids` is not a complete snapshot) and with how refresh rebuilds membership: **`prior_members` comes only from `prior.netuids`**, so a cleared-`netuids` LKG with intact `validity_map`/`rows` can drop grace state on the next writer cycle (**blocking: `never-expires`, `poisons-later-row`**). **`reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `netuids`**, so the new accept rule applies only on cold start, not on the reader reload path.\n\nRecommendation: either reject empty `netuids` on all read paths per rule 1, or normalize membership from `validity_map`/row netuids on load, mirror the guard in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, and add regression tests. Gate `next` remains `review` in the fixture after the post.",
