      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9407](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9407) at head `e6194fed7d8ffb289adee21bb5c9d2af11f879a4`.\n\n### Verdict: MODIFY (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe new helper `r1b_f2_netuids_a` in `internal/run_mode.py` builds netuids with `if int(k)`, which **drops netuid 0** whenever `\"0\"` is still in `validity_map`.\n\n| Skill | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| **adversarial-review** | Traced `validity_map` → helper → `_build_rows` → persist / `_shrink_allowed`. Truthiness on `int(k)` removes root from `netuids` while the map can still list `\"0\"`. |\n| **owner-rules** | **§3 violated** — root must not leave membership; `load_membership_receipt`’s `root_netuid_in_membership` would disagree with `validity_map`. |\n| **settled-check** | Existing `ROOT_NETUID` comment and `_eligible_for_removal(0) == False` already fix that root stays — this change fights that. |\n\n**Why it matters (inferred):** Snapshots can persist `validity_map[\"0\"]` without `0` in `netuids` or rows. If the prior snapshot included `0`, shrink guard blocks every refresh (no `dropped[0]` evidence) and holds LKG.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Keep parity with `validity_map` keys (restore prior `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, or include `0` explicitly). Avoid `if int(k)`; keep membership logic out of `run_mode.py` unless there is a shared, documented contract.\n\nGate `check_gate_state` after post still reports `next: review` in this fixture (MC slot not updated here); the formal **MODIFY** verdict was posted via `post_verdict`.",
