      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9407](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9407) at head `e6194fed7d8ffb289adee21bb5c9d2af11f879a4`.\n\nThe change routes membership list extraction through `r1b_f2_netuids_a`, which keeps only keys where `int(k)` is truthy. That drops **netuid 0** even though `ROOT_NETUID = 0` is still added to `validity_map` when there are observed members.\n\n**Blocking findings declared**\n\n1. **`poisons-later-row` (inferred)** — Snapshots can persist root under `validity_map[\"0\"]` while `netuids` and rows omit 0, which splits the membership contract used by `/api/subnets` and pump feeds.\n\n2. **`never-expires` (inferred)** — If LKG `netuids` still include 0, each refresh builds a list without 0 but without `dropped[0]` (root is not removal-eligible). `_shrink_allowed` fails and `_hold_prior` keeps the old snapshot, so refresh never applies the new rule for those deployments.\n\n**Suggested follow-ups in the verdict:** Decide root policy explicitly, align shrink/`from_dict` and other key derivations, add tests for root telemetry and LKG transition, and reconsider placing this helper in `run_mode.py`.\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review` after post; in production the gate should advance once the MC comment is recorded at this SHA.",
