unction import in `_compute_membership` is inconsistent with top-level imports elsewhere.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n| Input | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Non-numeric `validity_map` key | **inferred:** `int(x)` raises → refresh cycle error (same as prior `int(k)` line). |\n| Only `\"0\"` in `validity_map` | **inferred:** `netuids == []` → existing empty-membership branches in `SnapshotBuilder.build`. |\n| Large / negative int keys | **inferred:** `if k` only drops 0; negatives would remain (unchanged oddity vs prior). |\n\nNo **measured** path where this change alone causes overflow to `inf`/`NaN`, never-expiring grace rows, or blank picks via empty snapshot publish.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n- **Rule 3 (netuid 0 never removed):** **measured:** Removal *evidence* still cannot remove 0 from membership logic; this PR removes 0 only from the derived `netuids` list — consistent with `tradable.py` (root not a pick) but conflicts with shrink retention when LKG still contains 0.\n- **Rules 1, 2, 4, 5:** No new empty-snapshot reader path, chain-over-TMC unchanged, writer-only refresh unchanged.\n\n## Settled-check\n\n**guess:** Fixture repo has no roadmap/docs in scope; no settled doc contradicting tradable root exclusion. Shrink interaction with root is not obviously pre-decided in available files.\n",
