            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_compute_membership` now sets `netuids = r1b_f2_netuids_b(validity_map)` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`. `r1b_f2_netuids_b` returns `sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map.keys()) if k)`, which drops netuid **0** (and any non‑positive key) while `validity_map` can still retain the Root entry (`ROOT_NETUID = 0` is still merged into candidates when `observed_members` is non‑empty).\n\n**Measured:** `internal/subnets/tradable.py` documents that Root is never a tradable pick; `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` already treats `0 in snap.netuids` as a telemetry flag and scoring paths filter `int(n) > 0`. Centralizing Root exclusion at list build time matches that settled product shape.\n\n## P2 — unsafe shrink blocks shedding Root from persisted membership\n\n**Inferred:** For any LKG/prior snapshot whose `netuids` still contain `0` (possible under the old list builder), a refresh that correctly omits `0` in the new build produces `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.netuids) == {0}`. Root is never placed in `build.dropped` because `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`. `_shrink_allowed` therefore fails, `refresh_once` calls `_hold_prior`, and the worker **re‑publishes the prior list including 0** on every cycle until the on‑disk snapshot is replaced some other way.\n\n**Inferred:** Downstream readers (`get_netuids`, pump rows, `root_netuid_in_membership` in coverage receipts) can keep observing Root in membership long after the new helper would exclude it — bad state that later refreshes keep reading back via LKG hold.\n\n**Suggested fix (minimal):** Treat `{ROOT_NETUID}` dropped from `build.snapshot.netuids` as always safe in `_shrink_allowed`, and/or filter `0` out when loading `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` so migration does not fight the shrink gate. Add a focused test around prior-with-0 → refresh omits 0 without hold.\n\n## P3 — helper polish\n\n**Measured:** `r1b_f2_netuids_b` has no docstring or type hints unlike neighboring helpers in `tradable.py`. **Guess:** Renaming toward `tradable_membership_netuids(validity_map)` (or reusing the `int(n) > 0` predicate used in `membership_scoring_expected`) would align readability with the module header, but this is not blocking.\n\n## Edge values (adversarial trace)\n\n**Inferred:** Non‑numeric `validity_map` keys still raise in `int(x)` — same as the pre‑change comprehension; can abort `_compute_membership` / refresh loop iteration (pre‑existing). No new overflow/`inf`/`NaN` path in this two‑file diff.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `netuids` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_shrink_allowed` / `_hold_prior` / `get_netuids`; Root exclusion vs drop evidence | — |\n| owner-rules | Root not scored; membership receipts already flag `root_netuid_in_membership`; chain/grace rules unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | Excluding Root from tradable universe is already documented in `tradable.py` and enforced in coverage scoring filters | — |",
