            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `3a543a09` routes membership export through new `r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map)` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` in `_compute_membership` (**measured** from `get_pr_diff` and head read of `internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n## Blocking finding (P1): root netuid dropped from `snap.netuids` while it can remain in `validity_map`\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can keep `\"0\"` in `validity_map` when not dropped (`internal/subnet_universe.py` head lines ~336–374, `ROOT_NETUID = 0` comment at line 23).\n\n**Measured:** New helper (patch on `snapshot_coverage.py`):\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map):\n    return sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map) if max(k, 0))\n```\n\n**Inferred (Python semantics, not executed):** For integer `k`, `if max(k, 0)` is false when `k == 0` and true when `k > 0`, so netuid **0 is excluded** from the exported list even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`. That replaces the prior behavior of exporting every validity-map key.\n\n**Inferred consumers on the real publish path:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `UniverseSnapshot.netuids=tuple(netuids)` from this return value (head ~574–631). `load_membership_receipt` in `snapshot_coverage.py` sets `\"root_netuid_in_membership\": 0 in snap.netuids` (head ~88) and builds scoring expectations from `snap.netuids` filtered with `int(n) > 0` (~68–71). With 0 removed from `netuids`, root can be present in `validity_map` but absent from `snap.netuids`, so persisted snapshots and coverage receipts can disagree on root membership (**poisons-later-row**).\n\n**Inferred shrink interaction:** `_shrink_allowed` treats any netuid in `prior.netuids` missing from the new list as a shrink; root removal is never eligible (`_eligible_for_removal` returns false for `ROOT_NETUID`, head ~269–271). If prior snapshots include 0 in `netuids`, a refresh that omits 0 triggers unsafe-shrink hold (head ~296–303, ~724–733), which can stall universe updates relative to a fresh `validity_map` that still contains `\"0\"`.\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n- **P3:** Lazy import of `snapshot_coverage` inside `_compute_membership` on every membership resolve adds a circular coupling (`snapshot_coverage` already calls `subnet_universe` in `load_membership_receipt`); consider a neutral shared helper module or a documented `k >= 0` / include-root policy with a one-line docstring instead of `r1b_f2_netuids_c` without docs.\n- **P3:** If the intent is only to iterate `validity_map` without `.keys()` (\"key shape\"), the predicate should match prior membership export (include 0), e.g. `sorted(int(x) for x in validity_map)` or `if k >= 0` if negatives must be dropped—not `if max(k, 0)`.\n\n## Requested fix direction\n\nAlign export with documented root membership: either include 0 when `\"0\"` is in `validity_map`, or explicitly move `root_netuid_in_membership` (and any row build expectations) to read `validity_map` and add tests for the observed-members path with root present.\n\n| Claim | Label |\n| --- | --- |\n| Diff and head reads for `_compute_membership` / `SnapshotBuilder.build` | measured |\n| `max(k,0)` filter excludes `k==0` | inferred |\n| Receipt / shrink behavior when 0 missing from `netuids` | inferred |",
