          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nDelegation replaces inline `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map)` in `_compute_membership`. The helper is not ordering-only: it returns `sorted(x for x in keys if x)`, which **drops netuid 0** because `0` is falsy in Python (**measured**, `internal/chain_price/membership.py`). Base behavior included every validity_map key, including `\"0\"` (**measured**, base `internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Root netuid omission vs unsafe-shrink gate (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n- **measured**: `_compute_membership` still inserts root into `validity_map` when it stays a member (loop over `candidates` including `ROOT_NETUID`).\n- **measured**: `r1b_f2_netuids_d` excludes `0` from the returned list while `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map`.\n- **measured**: `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` always.\n- **measured**: `_shrink_allowed` rejects any publish where `prior.netuids - build.snapshot.netuids` contains a netuid without eligible drop evidence.\n- **inferred**: Workers whose LKG snapshot still lists `0` in `netuids` (prior persisted behavior) will produce builds whose `netuids` omit `0` but cannot satisfy `_shrink_allowed`; `refresh_once` retains LKG via `_hold_prior` (\"Unsafe shrink blocked\"), so membership refresh stops adopting the newly computed map/rows on every cycle.\n\n### P2 — Telemetry / API skew (**inferred**)\n\n- **inferred**: `load_membership_receipt` sets `root_netuid_in_membership` from `0 in snap.netuids` while root may still appear in `validity_map`, so receipt can under-report root membership after this change.\n- **inferred**: `universe_snapshot_feed_meta` majority heuristics use `len(snap.netuids)` against `validity_map` entries; excluding root from `netuids` only skews those ratios when root is a member.\n\n### P3 — Helper hygiene (**measured**)\n\n- **measured**: New helper has no docstring, no test in this diff, opaque name `r1b_f2_netuids_d`, and a one-line semicolon body—hard to prove equivalence to the old sort for future edits.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n\n- Make netuid list derivation match the documented root rule explicitly (either include `0` when `\"0\"` ∈ `validity_map`, or remove root from `validity_map` when excluding it from `netuids`), **and** teach `_shrink_allowed` / migration so LKG with legacy `0` in `netuids` is not permanently stuck.\n- Add a focused test around `_compute_membership` / refresh shrink for root + validity_map parity.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `r1b_f2_netuids_d` → `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` → `_shrink_allowed` / `refresh_once`; falsy filter removes root | — |\n| owner-rules | Root is special-cased in probe/removal paths; helper should not silently diverge from persisted `netuids` without a migration story | — |\n| settled-check | #1395 membership module ownership supports centralizing list logic; does not settle dropping root or shrink interaction | — |",
