            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line export filter in `_compute_membership` plus a comment in `tag.ts`. The Python change is meant to drop netuid **0** from the published `netuids` list while **0** can remain in `validity_map`. That collides with `_shrink_allowed` on any worker that already persisted **0** in `prior.netuids`, so the intended export never publishes.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Root export omit vs unsafe-shrink (P1, blocking)\n\n**Measured** (read at head): `_compute_membership` now builds:\n\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if k != str(0))`\n\n**Measured**: `_shrink_allowed` treats every `netuid ∈ prior.netuids \\ built.netuids` as a removal that must have eligible drop evidence; for `ROOT_NETUID`, `_eligible_for_removal` always returns `False`.\n\n**Inferred**: On a normal LKG where root was previously exported (old line included all `validity_map` keys, and `observed_members` adds `ROOT_NETUID` to candidates), the next refresh produces `built.netuids` without **0** but `prior.netuids` still contains **0**. **0** is not in `dropped`, so `_shrink_allowed` returns `False` → `refresh_once` replaces the build with `_hold_prior` (\"Unsafe shrink blocked\"). The worker keeps serving the old snapshot with **0** in `netuids`; the new export shape never lands on disk.\n\n**Inferred**: `load_membership_receipt()` already derives scoring netuids with `int(n) > 0` and exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`; this PR would flip that flag only if publish succeeded — but shrink blocking prevents the sync the title describes for existing deployments.\n\n**Fix direction (inferred)**: Treat root export normalization separately from chain-driven removal (e.g. exclude **0** from the shrink diff, or allow shrink when **0** is the only delta and still present in `validity_map`). Add/adjust a test around `refresh_once` with prior `netuids` containing **0**.\n\n### 2. `validity_map` / `netuids` split for root (P2)\n\n**Inferred**: **0** can remain in `validity_map` while absent from `netuids` and `_build_rows`, so persisted snapshots can carry root validity without a row. Align with owner rule **#3** (root never removed; universe 0–127) explicitly in code/comments so export semantics are clear.\n\n### 3. `review-gate-bot/bot/lib/tag.ts` (P3)\n\n**Measured**: Comment-only (`// pack-b: membership export shares tag epoch with universe refresh`); no behavioral change.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n- **#3**: Export omitting **0** while shrink logic treats omitting **0** as forbidden removal is inconsistent with \"never removed\" unless shrink is updated (finding 1).\n- **#1–#2, #4–#5**: Not exercised by this diff.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — shrink guard blocks publishing the new membership export for typical LKGs that include root in `netuids`.",
