      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9411 at head `c1f6dd954a04d4c762832899784321a88b7d3f96`.\n\n### Main issue (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe change drops netuid **0** from the exported `netuids` list:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if k != str(0))\n```\n\nOn workers whose last-known-good snapshot still has **0** in `prior.netuids` (normal today), the next refresh builds membership **without** **0** but `_shrink_allowed` treats that as a shrink. Root cannot satisfy removal evidence (`_eligible_for_removal` is always false for `ROOT_NETUID`), so refresh keeps `_hold_prior` (“Unsafe shrink blocked”) and **never publishes** the new export shape. That blocks the “membership export in sync” goal for existing deployments.\n\n### Secondary\n\n- **0** can stay in `validity_map` while missing from `netuids`/`rows` — clarify against owner rule **#3**.\n- `tag.ts` is comment-only; no behavioral change.\n\n### Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Shrink path vs root export filter | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule **#3** vs shrink semantics | — |\n| settled-check | No external settled doc in session | — |\n\n**Suggested fix:** Treat root export normalization separately from evidence-backed removals (e.g. exclude **0** from the shrink diff when it remains in `validity_map`), plus a `refresh_once` test with prior `netuids` containing **0**.",
