      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on PR 9412 @ `af9a6e08…`)\n\nThe change in `_compute_membership` is:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})\n```\n\n**Blocking issue:** `if int(k)` treats netuid **0** as falsy, so when `validity_map` contains `\"0\"` (which the same function can set for `ROOT_NETUID`), **0 is omitted from `netuids`** while the validity entry remains. That diverges from base (`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included 0), breaks consistency between `netuids`, `rows`, and `validity_map` on publish, and conflicts with **owner rule 3** (netuid 0 is never removed from membership). Declared blocking category: **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Fix direction:** dedupe/normalize with something like `sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()})` — do not filter with `if int(k)`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture environment; the formal MC comment was posted with the Skills table. After the author fixes and pushes a new head, the gate can advance on a fresh SHA.",
