            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change at the end of `_compute_membership` rebuilds `netuids` from `validity_map` keys using a set comprehension plus a truthiness filter on `int(k)`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `if int(k)` drops netuid 0 while it can remain in `validity_map` (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership adds root when there are observed members; the loop writes `validity_map[str(netuid)]` including for root, and `_eligible_for_removal` never removes root.\n\n**Measured:** New code:\n`netuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})`\n\n**Inferred:** In Python, `if int(k)` rejects `0`, so whenever key `\"0\"` is present, `netuids` and `_build_rows(netuids, …)` omit root while `validity_map` still carries `\"0\"`. That is inconsistent persisted/API state (membership list vs validity map / feed meta that compares `len(snap.netuids)` to validity entries). Prior head used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included 0.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Normalize/deduplicate without falsy filter, e.g. `sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map})`, or an explicit `try`/`except` around `int(k)` if skipping non-numeric keys is intended — do not use truthiness on `int(k)` if 0 is a valid member.\n\n### P3 — Set dedup alone does not explain the filter (**inferred**)\n\nKeys in this function are always `str(netuid)` from the candidate loop, so duplicate string forms for the same integer should not appear in `validity_map` from this path. The set mainly helps if foreign keys ever appear in a loaded map; the risky part is still `if int(k)`.\n\n## Extremes (not run — read-only review)\n\nNon-digit keys in `validity_map.keys()` would make `int(k)` raise and abort a refresh cycle (**inferred** `aborts-cycle`); not observed as produced by the loop, only via corrupted persistence.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `UniverseSnapshot` / `get_netuids`; truthiness on `int(k)` vs `ROOT_NETUID` | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain/membership semantics around root and grace unchanged by diff; this line affects who appears in shared universe rows | — |\n| settled-check | Fixture tree has no roadmap/docs to re-litigate; treated as open | — |",
