      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [#9412](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9412) at head `af9a6e08d6e0d56608d0b93aa35e479daa825d20`.\n\n**Why not PASS:** The new line is:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})\n```\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID` is `0`, and `_compute_membership` can keep `\"0\"` in `validity_map` while root is never eligible for removal.\n\n**Inferred:** `if int(k)` treats `0` as falsy, so netuid **0 is dropped from `netuids`** (and from `_build_rows`) even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`. That desyncs membership rows from the map and from helpers that compare `len(snap.netuids)` to validity entries — classified as **`poisons-later-row`**, which blocks PASS.\n\n**Recommendation:** Deduplicate with `sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map})` (no truthiness filter), or skip only non-numeric keys explicitly without excluding `0`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture session; the formal MC comment is on the PR. Author should fix the filter and push; MC will review the new head when it lands.",
