            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor moves member-netuid extraction from `_compute_membership` into `internal.run_mode.r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a`. The helper is not gated on run mode and **changes semantics**: it drops netuid **0** from `netuids` whenever key `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Netuid 0 excluded from published membership (owner rule 3)\n\n**Measured:** Base `_compute_membership` ended with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n**Measured:** Head replaces that with `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a`, defined (per PR patch) as:\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0`; the membership loop still adds root to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`, so `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map` while no longer appearing in `netuids`.\n\n**Inferred:** `/api/subnets` and persisted snapshots built via `_build_rows(netuids, …)` omit the root row even though validity still tracks it — contradicts **owner rule 3** (netuid 0 is never removed from membership). Telemetry in `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` explicitly records `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids`; this would read false after the change.\n\n### P1 — Unsafe-shrink gate can freeze membership updates\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.netuids)`. Netuid 0 is never placed in `dropped`.\n\n**Inferred:** Any prior snapshot whose `netuids` includes `0` (historical LKG or pre-change publishes) will produce a build that omits `0` without evidence; `_shrink_allowed` returns false and `refresh_once` retains LKG (`Unsafe shrink blocked`). Legitimate removals of other netuids on the same cycle are blocked as well because `0` is in the removed set without evidence.\n\n## Non-blocking\n\n- **P3:** Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` hot path; membership policy living in `run_mode.py` is a surprising seam for a generalization helper name (`r1b_*`) with no run-mode branch.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n`validity_map` with key `\"0\"` only: **measured** helper yields `[]` vs base `[0]` — can push empty-membership branches in `SnapshotBuilder.build`. No float overflow / NaN paths touched.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nKeep the helper on the **same** set as base (`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`), or gate a root-excluding variant behind an explicit run-mode flag with tests and owner sign-off. Do not silently filter `if int(k)` in the default production path.",
