      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on PR 9449 @ `0a71ea955f7f3def695d321688886de5a619a6c0`)\n\nThe refactor is not behavior-neutral. Moving extraction to `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` adds `if int(k)`, which **drops netuid 0** from `netuids` whenever `\"0\"` is still in `validity_map`.\n\n| Skill | Found |\n| --- | --- |\n| **adversarial-review** | Traced `_compute_membership` → `netuids` → `_build_rows`, `refresh_once`, and `_shrink_allowed`; base used all map keys, head excludes falsy `int(k)` (i.e. 0). |\n| **owner-rules** | **Rule 3:** root can vanish from `snap.netuids` while remaining in `validity_map` — treated as removal from published membership. |\n| **settled-check** | Nothing in scope settles “root out of `netuids`”; `snapshot_coverage` still tracks `root_netuid_in_membership` as `0 in snap.netuids`. |\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row` — priors that still list `0` in `netuids` will omit it on the next build without drop evidence, so `_shrink_allowed` can block refresh and leave LKG stuck (including blocking other legitimate shrinks on the same cycle).\n\n**Fix direction:** Keep base semantics in the default path (`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`), or gate a root-excluding variant behind an explicit run-mode flag with tests and owner sign-off — not a silent `if int(k)` in production.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture (MC verdict may not be reflected yet); Cursor/Ditto have not run on this head.",
