            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor moves membership netuid extraction into `internal/subnets/tradable.py` but changes semantics: the new helper drops netuid **0** from `netuids` whenever key `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`. Base at `882980b8` used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which **includes** 0.\n\n## Finding (P1) — root excluded from published membership\n\n**measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can store `\"0\"` in `validity_map` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` (root is not dropped via the negative path).\n\n**measured:** New helper:\n```python\ndef r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b(validity_map):\n    return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n`int(0)` is falsy, so `\"0\"` never appears in `netuids`.\n\n**inferred:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` builds `rows` only from `netuids`, persists `UniverseSnapshot.netuids`, and `load_membership_receipt` sets `root_netuid_in_membership` from `0 in snap.netuids`. After this change, root can remain in `validity_map` but disappear from `netuids`/rows/receipt telemetry.\n\n**inferred:** If a prior snapshot had `0 in prior.netuids` and a refresh omits 0 without removal evidence, `_shrink_allowed` treats 0 as an unsafe drop (`_eligible_for_removal(ROOT, …)` is always false) and can block **all** shrink handling, retaining LKG (`_hold_prior`) even when other netuids have valid drop evidence.\n\n**Owner rule 3:** Netuid 0 is never removed; universe is 128 (0–127). This diff removes 0 from the membership list surface.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nKeep extraction in `tradable.py` if desired, but membership derivation from `validity_map` must remain equivalent to base: include netuid 0 when present (e.g. drop the `if int(k)` filter, or use an explicit `>= 0` / `!=` check that does not exclude root). Do not reuse tradable pick filtering (`n > 0`) for universe membership keys.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**measured:** `validity_map` keys in this path are `str(netuid)` from numeric candidates; non-numeric keys would fail `int(k)` in both old and new code.\n\n**measured:** No overflow/`1e308`/NaN path in this two-line membership helper.\n\nNo new mc verdict at this SHA before this review.",
