      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9450 at `80a0cc9543b7ab56b01799e2de9a3646cda767f2`.\n\n### Core issue (P1)\n\nThe new helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` uses `if int(k)`, which **drops netuid 0** from `netuids` even when `\"0\"` is still in `validity_map`.\n\n**measured:** Base used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which includes 0. `_compute_membership` can still put root in `validity_map`, and removal logic never allows dropping `ROOT_NETUID`.\n\n**inferred:** That mismatch can leave `validity_map` tracking root while `netuids`, rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership` omit it, and can make `_shrink_allowed` treat an omitted 0 as an unsafe shrink and hold LKG when other netuids should drop.\n\nThis conflicts with **owner rule 3** (netuid 0 is never removed; universe 0–127).\n\n### Fix\n\nKeep the refactor in `tradable.py` if you want, but membership extraction must match base semantics: **do not** apply tradable’s `n > 0` filter here—include 0 when it is a key in `validity_map`.\n\n### Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Base vs head netuid list; consumers snapshot/shrink/receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 | — |\n| settled-check | Rule 3 standing | — |\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row`\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after `post_verdict`; the formal MODIFY comment is on the PR for this head.",
