            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe refactor routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d`, which **silently omits netuid 0** whenever key `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`. Base used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included root. That mismatch is a membership bug, not a harmless dedup.\n\n## Finding (P1, blocking)\n\n**`r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` treats netuid 0 as non-member** (`poisons-later-row`)\n\n- **Measured:** At head, `internal/chain_price/membership.py` defines:\n  `return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))` — in Python, `int(0)` is falsy, so `\"0\"` is filtered out.\n- **Measured:** Base `internal/subnet_universe.py` used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with no truthiness filter.\n- **Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty, sets `probe_val = None` for root, and `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `netuid == ROOT_NETUID`, so `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map` while not being dropped.\n- **Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` comment in `subnet_universe.py`: *\"membership adds it\"* (distinct from `get_member_netuids`, which excludes 0 from chain keys by design).\n- **Inferred:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` persists `netuids=tuple(netuids)` and `_build_rows(netuids, …)` — root in `validity_map` but absent from `netuids` yields a snapshot whose member list and rows omit netuid 0 while validity metadata still claims it, i.e. bad persisted state later readers consume (`get_snapshot`, `get_netuids`, pump rows, coverage `root_netuid_in_membership`).\n- **Owner rule 3:** Netuid 0 is never removed; universe is 0–127. Dropping 0 from the published `netuids` list violates this even when removal is “only” via filtering.\n\n**Fix direction:** Do not reuse the chain-scan “exclude 0” predicate on `validity_map` keys. Either keep the prior one-liner or use an explicit `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (and add a regression test with `\"0\"` in the map).\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n\n- **P3:** Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` hot path — style/consistency only.\n- **P3:** No test in this diff for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` / root retention.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n| Input | Entry | Cycle abort? | Poisons later? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `validity_map = {\"0\": entry, \"1\": entry}` | `_compute_membership` → `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` | **Inferred:** no throw | **Inferred:** yes — persisted `netuids` missing 0 |\n| `1e308`, `NaN`, `inf` | N/A — keys are string netuid ids from loop | N/A | N/A for this diff |\n\n## Settled-check\n\nNo settled doc/lock found in reviewed paths that authorizes dropping netuid 0 from universe `validity_map` extraction; existing comment and `_eligible_for_removal` point the opposite way.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → persist; `if int(k)` drops 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3 (netuid 0 never removed); rule 1 adjacent (incomplete member list vs map) | — |\n| settled-check | No prior decision to exclude 0 from map-derived netuids | — |",
