      "finalText": "**Verdict posted: FAIL** on head `0b569f846468d4bf9538816cedbc60f8936e75fe` ([PR 9452](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9452)).\n\n### Blocking finding (`poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe new helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` is:\n\n```python\nreturn sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\nBecause `int(0)` is falsy in Python, **netuid 0 is dropped** whenever `\"0\"` is in `validity_map`. **Measured:** base `_compute_membership` used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with no filter.\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to candidates when there are observed members, never allows removal via `_eligible_for_removal`, and the file comment states universe **membership adds** root (unlike `get_member_netuids`, which excludes 0 from chain storage keys by design).\n\n**Inferred:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` publishes `netuids` and `_build_rows(netuids, …)` from that list, so you can persist a snapshot where `validity_map` includes `\"0\"` but `netuids`/rows omit root — bad state for `get_snapshot`, pump membership rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership` telemetry. That conflicts with **owner rule 3** (netuid 0 is never removed).\n\n### Fix\n\nDo not apply the chain-scan “exclude 0” rule to `validity_map` keys. Restore `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (or equivalent) and add a test with `\"0\"` in the map.\n\nGate `next` remains **`await_cursor_ditto`** / follow-on steps per fixture after MC FAIL; Cursor and Ditto still need to run at this head before suite/Replit.",
