            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `_compute_membership`: derive `netuids` from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, excluding netuid `0` (`ROOT_NETUID`) from the published membership list. Intent matches existing D5/scoring seams that treat root as non-member (**inferred** from `ROOT_NETUID` comment and `load_membership_receipt` filtering `int(n) > 0`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Root drop is blocked by `_shrink_allowed` (**measured** / **inferred** downstream)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_compute_membership` ends with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, so a positive root entry in `validity_map` no longer appears in `build.snapshot.netuids`. `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`, and root is never placed in `dropped` (only negative + eligible removals). `_shrink_allowed` requires every netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)` to have eligible drop evidence; missing evidence for netuid `0` forces `False`.\n\n**Measured:** `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` then replaces the build with `_hold_prior(..., \"Unsafe shrink blocked — retained last-known-good universe\")`, republishing the **prior** snapshot unchanged.\n\n**Inferred:** Any LKG/persisted snapshot that already lists netuid `0` (possible under base, which included `\"0\"` in `netuids` when root sat in `validity_map`) will **never** shed root on refresh after this change; later cycles keep reading and publishing the old list (`get_netuids()`, persisted JSON, pump rows). Telemetry `root_netuid_in_membership` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` suggests this state is tracked because it occurs.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Treat explicit root exclusion as a safe shrink (e.g. skip `ROOT_NETUID` in the `_shrink_allowed` loop, or omit root from `prior_members` when diffing), or remove root from `validity_map` in the same helper so prior/build semantics stay aligned.\n\n### P3 — `validity_map` may still contain `\"0\"` while `netuids` omits 0 (**measured**)\n\nOrphan validity entry for root vs membership list; low severity if root is excluded everywhere, but inconsistent for consumers that iterate map keys.\n\n### No float / overflow path (**measured**)\n\nChange is integer netuid key filtering only; no new multiply or grace clock on floats.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `refresh_once` / `_shrink_allowed`; root filter triggers hold-prior loop | — |\n| owner-rules | Root not probed/scored; membership helper centralization matches D5 comment at file top (**inferred** from repo text) | — |\n| settled-check | Aligns with existing `int(n) > 0` receipt/scoring filters; not re-litigating root policy (**inferred**) | — |",
