      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on PR 9453 @ `24f63b56`)\n\nThe diff is a single line in `_compute_membership`: membership `netuids` are built from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, which drops netuid **0** (`ROOT_NETUID`). That matches how scoring already treats root (e.g. `load_membership_receipt` uses `int(n) > 0` and tracks `root_netuid_in_membership`).\n\n**Blocking issue (poisons-later-row):** **Measured** in code: `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every netuid removed from the prior snapshot. Root can never be `_eligible_for_removal` and is not added to `dropped`, so if LKG already contains `0`, a refresh that would remove it is treated as an unsafe shrink and **`_hold_prior` keeps publishing the old snapshot**. Later cycles therefore keep serving netuid 0 via `get_netuids()`, persistence, and pump rows until shrink logic explicitly allows shedding root (or root is cleared another way).\n\n**P3:** **Measured** — `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map` while absent from `netuids` (orphan validity entry).\n\nNo new float/overflow/grace-clock paths in this change.\n\n**Next (gate):** `check_gate_state` still shows `next: review` in the fixture; Cursor/Ditto/suite follow the usual gate order after MC is recorded on the PR.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | `_compute_membership` → `refresh_once` / `_shrink_allowed` blocks root removal from LKG | — |\n| owner-rules | Aligns with in-code ROOT/D5 membership intent | — |\n| settled-check | Extends existing root-exclusion policy, not a new cap/grace debate | — |",
