            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR 9454 routes `_compute_membership` netuid extraction through `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`. The helper changes membership semantics: it drops netuid **0** from `snap.netuids` while `_compute_membership` can still place `\"0\"` in `validity_map`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Netuid 0 omitted from universe `netuids` (**poisons-later-row**, owner rule 3)\n\n**Measured (diff, base vs head):** Base `_compute_membership` ended with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\nHead replaces this with `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f(validity_map)` defined as:\n`return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`.\n\n**Measured (head `internal/subnet_universe.py`):** When `observed_members` is non-empty, `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)` with `ROOT_NETUID = 0`; positive root entries remain in `validity_map` under key `\"0\"` (root is never eligible for `dropped` — `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`).\n\n**Inferred (consumer trace):** With the new helper, netuid 0 is excluded from `netuids` whenever it is only present as `0` / `\"0\"` (because `if int(k)` is false for zero). Effects on the real publish path (`SnapshotBuilder.build` → `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=tuple(netuids), …)` → `_atomic_persist`):\n- `load_membership_receipt()` sets `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids` → **False** even when `validity_map` still contains `\"0\"`.\n- `_build_rows(netuids, …)` never materializes a row for netuid 0 when it is absent from `netuids`, while `validity_map` may still record root membership.\n\n**Inferred (upgrade vs greenfield):** If prior LKG already lists `0`, `_shrink_allowed` may block publishing the shrink (no drop evidence for root). On greenfield or prior without `0`, the inconsistent snapshot can persist without shrink guard firing.\n\nThis contradicts owner rule **3** (netuid 0 is never removed from membership) and writes disk state where `validity_map` and `netuids` disagree on root — bad state later cycles and readers consume.\n\n**Fix direction:** Either keep universe extraction identical to base (include 0), or use an explicit predicate (e.g. `>= 0`) if filtering was intended for non-netuid keys — not truthiness on `int(k)`. If the helper is scoring-only, do not use it in `_compute_membership`.\n\n### P3 — Lazy import inside `_compute_membership`\n\n**Measured:** Per-cycle `from internal.council.snapshot_coverage import r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` inside `_compute_membership`. Prefer module-level import for clarity; not blocking alone.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map[\"0\"]` → helper → persisted `snap.netuids` / receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 3: root must remain in membership surface | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in available repo slice for `r1b_*`; regression vs base one-liner | — |\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — do not merge until netuid 0 behavior matches the prior membership contract (or explicit owner-approved semantics with tests).",
