      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on PR 9454 at head `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\n### Main issue (blocking: `poisons-later-row`, owner rule 3)\n\n**Measured:** Base `_compute_membership` used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which includes netuid **0** when `\"0\"` is in the map. The new helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` uses `if int(k)`, which **drops 0** because `int(0)` is falsy.\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to candidates and can keep `\"0\"` in `validity_map`; root is never eligible for `dropped`.\n\n**Inferred:** Published `UniverseSnapshot.netuids` can omit 0 while `validity_map` still has `\"0\"`. That makes `root_netuid_in_membership` false in `load_membership_receipt()`, skips a root row in `_build_rows`, and conflicts with “netuid 0 is never removed” for greenfield or non-shrink paths.\n\n**Fix:** Keep universe extraction equivalent to the old one-liner (include 0), or use an explicit filter—not truthiness on `int(k)`. If this helper is scoring-only, don’t call it from `_compute_membership`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; the formal MODIFY comment is on the PR. Next step for the author is to fix netuid 0 handling and push a new head for re-review.",
