      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9454](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9454) at `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\n### What changed (measured)\nThe PR centralizes membership list derivation in `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f`, which returns `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`. That **drops netuid 0**, whereas base used every validity_map key (including `\"0\"`).\n\n### Blocking concern (inferred → `poisons-later-row`)\nIf last-known-good `prior.netuids` still contains **0** (normal under base when root stayed in `validity_map`), a refresh builds a list **without** 0 while root is **not** in `dropped` (`_eligible_for_removal(ROOT_NETUID, …)` is hard-coded false). **`_shrink_allowed` then blocks the shrink**, `refresh_once` keeps the prior via `_hold_prior` (degraded, `refresh_incomplete=True`), and later cycles can keep reading that stuck state instead of publishing the root-stripped membership—gating paths that honor degraded/incomplete receipts.\n\n### Ask\nAlign shrink policy with intentional root exclusion (e.g. exempt `ROOT_NETUID` from the shrink-evidence check or a one-shot LKG migration + test), and state clearly in the PR that this is behavioral, not a pure refactor.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | shrink guard vs root drop on refresh | — |\n| owner-rules | root/grace rules; no shrink fix in diff | — |\n| settled-check | no settled R1b/shrink doc in session fixture | — |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; follow your channel’s gate runner if it should advance on MC MODIFY.",
