be-True to `MAX_NETUIDS`) (**measured**). If parallel ordering is the issue, prefer xdist grouping or splitting the provider vs builder assertions rather than skipping the whole case (**inferred**).\n\n### P4 — Parallelization not evidenced in the diff (**measured**)\n\nChanged files are `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` only; no worker matrix / shard wiring appears in the PR file list returned by the gate (**measured**). Title should match the harness change or the workflow commit should be included for review.\n\n## Adversarial production trace\n\nNo numeric inputs, persistence writers, or refresh loops were modified. Extreme-value paths (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`, grace eligibility, `_merge_sources` chain-wins) behave as on base (**inferred** from unchanged `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head). No finding that rows never expire, overflow to inf/NaN, abort a cycle, or poison later rows from this diff.\n\n## Gate\n\n`check_gate_state`: suite already **clean** at this head; MC verdict was **missing** — this comment supplies it.",
