            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `2dbb5f5` adds `_token_count_guard` and an early check in `_eligible_for_removal`. The call site always passes literal `0`, so the guard fails every time and **no netuid can ever be dropped** after the existing probe/grace checks. That contradicts the PR title (gate removals on audit-trail `token_count`) and the module’s stated rule that membership leaves only on cycle evidence after 48h grace.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `_token_count_guard(0)` disables all removals (**blocking**)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_eligible_for_removal` begins with:\n\n```python\nif not _token_count_guard(0):\n    return False\n```\n\nand `_token_count_guard` returns `token_count > 0`.\n\n**Inferred:** For every `(netuid, evidence, now)`, `_token_count_guard(0)` is false, so `_eligible_for_removal` returns false before `ROOT_NETUID`, probe, or `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` logic runs.\n\n**Inferred (real entry point):** `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership`. When `validity == \"negative\"`, the branch `if validity == \"negative\" and _eligible_for_removal(...)` never adds to `dropped`; those netuids stay in `validity_map` and remain in `netuids` indefinitely instead of leaving after grace.\n\n**Inferred:** `_shrink_allowed` also never sees eligible drops for grace-satisfied negatives, so unsafe-shrink protection no longer matches the intended drop path—membership **never shrinks** via the removal pipeline.\n\nMaps to blocking: **never-expires** (negative members never leave `netuids` after grace), **poisons-later-row** (persisted LKG and pump/API rows keep deregistered netuids forever).\n\n### P2 — No audit-trail `token_count` wired\n\n**Measured:** The only change in the PR is in `internal/subnet_universe.py`; no read of audit-trail fields, env, or receipt `token_count` appears in the touched path or sibling files exposed in this fixture.\n\n**Inferred:** The guard does not implement “gate removals on token_count for audit trails”; it is a constant-false gate.\n\n### P3 — Signature readability\n\n**Measured:** Tool output redacts part of the `def _token_count_guard(...)` line. **Guess:** Redaction may hide a valid `(token_count: int) -> bool` signature; if the committed line is actually missing `)`, import of `internal.subnet_universe` would fail (**aborts-cycle**). Confirm in GitHub UI at full line text.\n\n## Owner alignment\n\n**Inferred:** `_compute_membership` docstring and `load_membership_receipt` inactive/expected split assume negatives can progress to removal after grace; this diff freezes everyone in `netuids` while still marking validity—misaligned with D5 shared-universe honesty.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `0` through `_eligible_for_removal` → `_compute_membership` → `refresh_once` / persist | — |\n| owner-rules | Removal-after-grace and membership receipt semantics conflict with always-false guard | — |\n| settled-check | No prior MC verdict at this SHA; not re-litigating D5 alignment itself | — |\n\n## Requested fix direction\n\nPass the **audit-trail token count** (or the intended feature flag) into `_token_count_guard`, not literal `0`. Add/adjust tests so a grace-satisfied negative with sufficient token count can drop and `_shrink_allowed` can succeed when evidence is complete.",
