          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `_compute_membership`: when the registration probe pass is incomplete and a candidate netuid has no entry in `probe_map`, the code now sets `probe_val` to `None` if `TMC_API_KEY` is present (after strip), otherwise `False`. Base always used `None` in that branch.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — PR title vs signal source (**inferred**)\n\nTitle says \"read **api_key header**\"; the change only consults `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` via `_api_key_present`. Nothing in this diff reads a request header or shares the same resolution path as `fetchers.taomarketcap` (not present in the review fixture). If production supplies the key only via header on web requests, worker-side membership may not see it and will always take the `False` branch (**guess** unless env is documented as canonical).\n\n### P1 — Synthetic chain `False` without observation (**measured** / **inferred**)\n\nReal entry: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_merge_sources`.\n\nWhen `probe_complete` is false and `netuid not in probe_map` (e.g. probe deadline returns `{}`, False from `_default_probe_fetch`), the no-key branch sets `probe_val=False` even though no registration read occurred for that netuid.\n\n`_merge_sources` then hits `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False`, which applies the owner comment \"**complete** chain read\" logic and sets `validity=\"negative\"` with a fresh `negative_since` (see head `internal/subnet_universe.py`). That entry is persisted in `validity_map` and affects later refreshes and scoring receipts (`load_membership_receipt` / inactive netuids). That is bad state written for later cycles without a real probe observation — not merely a degraded hold.\n\nKeyed deployments: this branch still yields `None`, same as base — no improvement there; the behavior change is entirely for missing/blank `TMC_API_KEY`.\n\n### P3 — No regression test (**measured**)\n\nDiff is one production file only; no test updates in the PR.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nThe no-key path fabricates chain-negative probe evidence on incomplete probes. That conflicts with the in-file owner rule and can poison persisted membership state. MODIFY: gate probe gap filling on actual probe completeness (keep `None` when unobserved), and if TMC pagination gaps need the API key, resolve the key the same way TMC fetch does (header + env), with tests for keyed vs unkeyed incomplete probe/TMC combinations.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Incomplete `probe_map` + absent `TMC_API_KEY` → synthetic `probe_val=False` → negative + `negative_since` in persisted map | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-negative path requires a complete chain read; synthetic `False` bypasses that | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture; treated as open design | — |",
            "blocking": [
              "poisons-later-row"
            ],
            "headSha": "a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e",
            "skills": [
              {
