      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9442](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9442) at `a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e`.\n\n**Headline:** When the registration probe is incomplete and a netuid is missing from `probe_map`, the no-`TMC_API_KEY` path sets `probe_val=False` without any chain read. That flows through `_merge_sources` as a chain negative, sets `negative_since`, and persists into `validity_map` — **poisons-later-row** (declared on the verdict).\n\n**Also:** The title mentions an **api_key header**, but the diff only checks **`TMC_API_KEY` in the environment**, not header resolution aligned with TMC fetch.\n\n**Keyed deploys:** With a present env key, this branch still yields `None` (same as base); the behavior change is only when the key is absent/blank.\n\nGate fixture still shows `mc: missing` and `next: review` after post; the tool reported `posted: true`. Cursor/Ditto review is the next gate step once MC is recorded on the real PR.",
