            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `d764649` adds `_password_ok` and calls it from `_eligible_for_removal` before the existing falsy and `fromisoformat` checks. The real entry path is unchanged in shape: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_eligible_for_removal` / `_shrink_allowed` (**measured** from `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — PR title / behavior mismatch (**inferred**)\n\nThe title claims the helper \"validates negative_since **formatting**.\" `_password_ok` only returns `len(password or \"\") >= 1`. It does not validate ISO-8601 or any timestamp shape; formatting is still enforced only by the existing `datetime.fromisoformat` try/except block (**measured** at head lines ~279–288). Any non-empty garbage string still passes `_password_ok`.\n\n### P2 — Misleading name and wrong abstraction (**inferred**)\n\n`_password_ok` lives on the universe shrink / grace path and is fed `str(evidence.negative_since)`. That name suggests credential checking, not timestamp hygiene, and will mislead future edits in a safety-critical gate (`_shrink_allowed` blocks unsafe shrinks).\n\n### P3 — Redundant check + `str(None)` footgun (**inferred**)\n\nFor `Optional[str]` evidence, `_password_ok(str(evidence.negative_since))` is redundant with `if not evidence.negative_since` for `\"\"` (both reject). For `None`, `str(None)` is `\"None\"` (length ≥ 1), so `_password_ok` returns True and the code relies on the **next** falsy check — fragile if someone reorders or drops that line.\n\n### Adversarial extremes (**inferred**, no execution)\n\n| Input | `_password_ok` | Falsy check | `fromisoformat` | vs base |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `None` | pass (`\"None\"`) | fail | — | same outcome |\n| `\"\"` | fail | fail | — | same |\n| valid ISO from `_now_iso()` | pass | pass | pass (if grace met) | same |\n| `\"not-a-date\"` | pass | pass | fail → not eligible | same |\n\nNo new overflow / float paths; no change to `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` arithmetic (**measured** constant 172800).\n\n## Conclusion\n\nMODIFY: drop the misnamed helper or replace it with an explicit, well-named guard (e.g. reject missing/blank `negative_since` **before** any `str()` coercion, and keep ISO parsing where it already is). Add a targeted test on `_eligible_for_removal` if behavior is meant to change.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `negative_since` through refresh → membership → removal; extremes above | — |\n| owner-rules | Shrink still gated by `_shrink_allowed` + probe False + grace; chain-merge logic untouched | — |\n| settled-check | Invalid/unparseable `negative_since` already blocked removal at base; no fixture docs to cite | — |",
