            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change: `_bearer_ok` plus an early return in `_eligible_for_removal` when `AUTH_BEARER` is set but does not look like an HTTP `Authorization` bearer value (`None` allowed; otherwise case-insensitive `bearer ` prefix).\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured** from `internal/subnet_universe.py` at `fb651d3e`: worker refresh path `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` marks `dropped` only when `validity == \"negative\"` and `_eligible_for_removal`; publish shrink is gated again in `_shrink_allowed`, which calls the same helper per removed netuid. The new check runs on both paths.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n| Input | Effect | Label |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `AUTH_BEARER` unset (`None`) | `_bearer_ok` true; removal still requires `probe is False`, `negative_since`, and ≥ `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (48h) | **measured** |\n| `AUTH_BEARER=\"\"` or non-`bearer ` value | `_bearer_ok` false → never eligible for removal → `_shrink_allowed` false → `_hold_prior` retains LKG | **measured** |\n| `AUTH_BEARER=\"Bearer <token>\"` | Prefix ok; chain/grace rules unchanged | **measured** |\n| `ROOT_NETUID` | Still hard false before bearer check | **measured** |\n| Float/`1e308`/NaN paths | Not on this code path | **measured** N/A |\n\nNo **measured** path where a bad float poisons a later row or aborts a refresh loop; failures defer to existing `_hold_prior` / degraded handling.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **P3 (inferred)** — Fail-open when `AUTH_BEARER` is unset vs fail-closed when set to a malformed value. Consistent with “only gate shrink when auth material is present,” but ops should know empty string blocks shrink indefinitely.\n2. **P3 (guess)** — If production sets `AUTH_BEARER` to a raw secret without the `Bearer ` prefix, universe shrink would never pass `_eligible_for_removal` until the env is fixed. Acceptable if deploy always mirrors the full header value; otherwise document or normalize.\n\nNeither is an accidental grace/timer bug; no blocking categories declared.\n\n## Owner alignment\n\n**Inferred** from existing module comments: chain-negative + grace still drive removal evidence; bearer is an additional shrink safety latch aligned with existing “unsafe shrink blocked” behavior, not a bypass of probe/negative_since rules.\n",
