            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change: `_eligible_for_removal` now uses `grace = STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` only when the effective client secret (env `CLIENT_SECRET` or `DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET` via `_client_secret_default`) is not the literal string `\"unset\"`; otherwise `grace = 0`. Entry points unchanged: `_compute_membership` (drop into `dropped`) and `_shrink_allowed` (block unsafe shrink in `refresh_once`).\n\n## Adversarial trace (measured / inferred)\n\n| Check | Label | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Real entry path | **measured** | `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` / `_shrink_allowed` → `_eligible_for_removal`. |\n| `grace = 0` | **inferred** | When effective secret is `\"unset\"`, removal eligibility is `(now - started).total_seconds() >= 0` after existing guards (root, probe not False, parseable `negative_since`). Does not skip evidence requirements. |\n| `grace = 172800` | **inferred** | When effective secret ≠ `\"unset\"`, behavior matches base (48h). |\n| Float / overflow | **measured** | No new float inputs or multiplies; datetime delta only. |\n| Never-expire removal | **inferred** | No path sets infinite grace or disables the time comparison; negatives still become eligible after `grace` seconds. |\n| Poison / abort | **inferred** | Faster shrink when unset secret does not write corrupt validity entries; `_shrink_allowed` still requires per-netuid evidence. |\n\n## Non-blocking notes (P3)\n\n- **inferred**: Diff adds no tests for the `CLIENT_SECRET` / default branch; full-repo pytest should confirm CI (typically no secret) still passes.\n- **inferred**: Deployments that leave the effective secret at `\"unset\"` will allow immediate shrink eligibility (0s grace) rather than 48h—consistent with the PR title; production should set a real secret if 48h shrink protection is required.\n- **guess**: `DEFAULT_CLIENT_SECRET` is the string `\"unset\"` (redacted in tooling); if it were any othe