            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once`: the non-writer branch calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` but no longer returns, so execution falls through into the writer refresh path.\n\n## Finding (P1) — reader path can refresh/publish\n\n**measured:** At base, when `not is_universe_refresh_writer()`, `refresh_once` returns `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and never acquires `_refresh_lock` or runs `_builder.build` / `_publish`.\n\n**measured:** At head, the same branch only invokes `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and then continues to `if not self._refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False)` and the full build/publish block (including `_publish(built)` with default `persist=True`).\n\n**measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` docstring: \"Only worker processes may refresh/publish; web reloads persisted snapshots.\" `ensure_universe_reader()` docstring: \"never refresh/publish.\"\n\n**inferred:** Any caller of `refresh_once()` on a non-writer process (web / `RUN_MODE` not worker) that wins the non-blocking lock can run TMC pagination + chain registration probe and atomically persist `subnet_universe.json`, racing the dedicated worker and violating the split ownership model. That is bad state on disk that other processes reload — **poisons-later-row**.\n\n**inferred:** PR title (\"share refresh work across web and worker\") suggests coordinated reload, not duplicate publishers. The likely intended shape is reload-for-all then **return for readers** (restore `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` or `return self._snapshot` after reload), or move shared reload outside the writer-only guard — not drop the return alone.\n\n**inferred:** Worker-only call sites in this module (`ensure_refresh_loop`, `kick_refresh_async` writer branch) behave the same as base when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true; regression is confined to the non-writer `refresh_once` contract, which base enforced and head does not.\n\n## Owner rules / settled\n\n**measured:** No change to 48h grace, chain-wins merge, or shrink guards in this diff.\n\n**inferred:** Settled split (worker publishes, web `ensure_universe_reader` reloads) is contradicted if non-writer `refresh_once` can publish.\n\n## Requested fix\n\nRestore an early return on the non-wwriter branch after disk reload, **or** explicitly reload then `return self._snapshot` before the refresh lock, with a test that web/non-writer `refresh_once` never calls `_publish`.",
