      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on PR 9401 @ `3d7148d`)\n\nThe diff drops `return` from the non-writer branch of `refresh_once`:\n\n```709:712:internal/subnet_universe.py\n    def refresh_once(self) -> UniverseSnapshot:\n        if not is_universe_refresh_writer():\n            self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()\n        if not self._refresh_lock.acquire(blocking=False):\n```\n\n**measured:** On base, that branch was `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()`, so web/read-only processes never entered `_refresh_lock`, `SnapshotBuilder.build`, or `_publish`.\n\n**measured:** On head, after reload the method continues into the full writer refresh path, including `_publish(built)` with default `persist=True`.\n\n**inferred:** That conflicts with `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (“only worker … may refresh/publish”) and with `ensure_universe_reader()` (“never refresh/publish”). If anything calls `refresh_once()` on a non-writer and wins the non-blocking lock, it can persist `subnet_universe.json` and race the worker — declared blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Suggested fix:** After reload on the reader path, return again (`return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` or reload then `return self._snapshot`) before the refresh lock; add or keep a test that non-writer `refresh_once` never publishes.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Base vs head non-writer path through build/publish | — |\n| owner-rules | Worker-only publish seam; grace/merge unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | Settled web-reload / worker-publish split undermined by missing return | — |\n\nGate `next` still shows `review` in the fixture after post; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow once MC is recorded at this SHA on the live PR.",
