            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line control-flow change in `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once`: when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, the method still calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` but no longer returns immediately afterward; execution continues to the existing non-blocking `_refresh_lock` acquire and (if acquired) the full build/publish path.\n\n## Entry-point trace (measured)\n\n- **`ensure_background_refresh()`** (measured at head): writer → `ensure_refresh_loop()` + `kick_refresh_async()`; non-writer → **`ensure_universe_reader()`** only (`reload_from_disk_if_stale`), never `refresh_once`.\n- **`refresh_once()` callers** (measured in `internal/subnet_universe.py`): `_refresh_loop` and the async kick thread inside `kick_refresh_async`. Both are only started when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true (`ensure_refresh_loop` guard; `kick_refresh_async` early return on non-writer).\n- **`is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (measured): returns true under CI/pytest (`_ci_or_test()`), else `internal.run_mode.is_worker_mode()`.\n\nProduction web/split read path therefore does not invoke `refresh_once` today; the diff does not alter the writer (`RUN_MODE=worker`) path at all.\n\n## Adversarial / extremes\n\nNo membership numeric inputs change (no `1e308`, grace multiply, validity merge edits). The change is concurrency/role gating only.\n\n**Inferred hazard (not a production entry point today):** if a non-writer process ever called `refresh_once()` directly, it would reload disk, then could acquire its **process-local** `_refresh_lock` and run `_builder.build` + `_publish`, conflicting with the docstring on `ensure_universe_reader` / `is_universe_refresh_writer` (web reload-only). That diverges from `kick_refresh_async`, which reloads and returns on non-writer without attempting refresh.\n\n**Inferred intended win (same-process contention):** after reload, a non-writer caller that hits a held `_refresh_lock` returns `self._snapshot` (post-reload), matching the old early-return outcome when a writer refresh is in flight in the same process.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nNo edits to 48h removal grace (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`), chain-wins negative probe merge, shrink guards, or D5 shared-universe semantics. Split ownership (worker refresh/publish vs web disk reload) remains enforced at **`ensure_background_refresh`** boot wiring.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAcceptable as a narrow coordination tweak given traced boot paths. Optional follow-up (not blocking): after reload on non-writer, either return before build (preserve strict read-only) or document that `refresh_once` is writer-only API and add an explicit `is_universe_refresh_writer()` guard before `_builder.build` if web must never publish.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `ensure_background_refresh` → reader vs writer refresh; no numeric poison paths | — |\n| owner-rules | Split refresh vs reload unchanged at boot; membership rules untouched | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture scope for this hunk | — |",
