            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `kick_refresh_async`: non-writers take the async thread path when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set; otherwise behavior matches base (sync `reload_from_disk_if_stale` + return).\n\n## Guard removed (diff flag)\n\n**Measured:** Base had `if not is_universe_refresh_writer(): reload; return`. Head replaces it with `if not is_universe_refresh_writer() and not os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\"): reload; return`.\n\n**Measured:** Without the env var, non-writers still hit the same reader early-return — no default relaxation.\n\n**Inferred:** With the env var, the only change vs base is *async* scheduling: the daemon thread calls `refresh_once()`, which **still** begins with `if not is_universe_refresh_writer(): return reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — no TMC/probe build and no `_publish` on web.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Sev | Label | Finding |\n|----|-----|-------|---------|\n| F1 | P2 | **measured** | PR title/imply \"schedule work on idle web workers\" but `refresh_once` / `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (RUN_MODE worker only) are unchanged. Opt-in env therefore does not enable universe refresh/publish on web — only moves disk reload off the caller thread. If full refresh on idle web was intended, this diff is incomplete (needs aligned guard in `refresh_once` or shared helper, plus tests). |\n| F2 | P3 | **measured** | `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` uses raw `os.environ.get` truthiness (unlike `run_mode` flags). Values like `0`/`false` would still enable the async path. |\n| F3 | P3 | **inferred** | `ensure_background_refresh()` still routes non-writers to `ensure_universe_reader()` only — no `kick_refresh_async`. Benefit depends on other callers not in this one-file diff; worth confirming wiring in the same rollout. |\n\n## Owner / membership rules\n\n**Measured:** No edits to `_merge_sources`, grace (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`), or shrink guards — chain-wins / 48h removal logic unchanged.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**Inferred:** Non-writer + env does not push `1e308`/`inf` through membership math here; publish path remains unreachable on web. Extra kick threads only repeat reader reload — no new `never-expires` / `poisons-later-row` class issue identified.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nClarify intent: (A) async disk reload only → document env + consider explicit off parsing; (B) idle web should run full refresh → extend writer gate consistently in `refresh_once` (and boot path if needed) with tests.",
