      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) at `8595d8fd288d013e8f2f75b16fb5c3bff29c0356`.\n\n**What changed:** `kick_refresh_async` only skips the reader early-return when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set (in addition to the existing writer path). Without that env var, non-writers still sync-call `reload_from_disk_if_stale` and return — same as base.\n\n**Why MODIFY:** The diff relaxes the kick gate but **`refresh_once` still treats non-writers as read-only** (`is_universe_refresh_writer()` → `RUN_MODE=worker` only). With the env var, the new behavior is an **async** disk reload, not a full universe build/publish on idle web. That looks misaligned with the PR title unless the intent is only “don’t block the request thread on reload.”\n\n**Also noted (P3):** raw env truthiness for `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB`, and `ensure_background_refresh()` still never calls `kick_refresh_async` on the web path in this file.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | kick → thread → `refresh_once` still reader-only on web | — |\n| owner-rules | no membership/grace/shrink edits | — |\n| settled-check | no settled doc in fixture for this flag | — |\n\nGate **next** still reads `review` in the fixture after post; Cursor/Ditto are up next once MC is recorded on your side.",
