            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line gate in `kick_refresh_async`: when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, non-writer (web) processes skip the early return and spawn the existing daemon kick thread instead of calling `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` synchronously on the caller thread.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Scheduled work on web is still reader-only (measured + inferred)\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` remains `is_worker_mode()` only (lines 283–292). The kick thread calls `refresh_once()`, which on non-writers immediately delegates to `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (lines 710–712) — no `_builder.build`, no `_publish`.\n\n**Inferred:** With `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB`, web workers do not gain universe build/publish; they only offload disk reload to `subnet-universe-kick`. That matches the docstring on `is_universe_refresh_writer` (“web reloads persisted snapshots”) but is easy to misread from the PR title (“schedule work”) as full refresh. If the intent is async reload only, say so in a comment next to the env check; if the intent is build on idle web, `refresh_once` must be updated in a follow-up without breaking the writer/publish split.\n\n### P2 — Kick no longer waits for reload when the flag is set (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** Base behavior on non-writer: synchronous `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` before return. Head behavior with truthy `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB`: return immediately after starting the thread.\n\n**Inferred:** Any caller that invokes `kick_refresh_async()` and then reads `get_snapshot()` in the same request assumes the old synchronous contract and can briefly serve pre-reload memory state until the thread finishes. Worth documenting or ensuring callers use `ensure_universe_reader()` when they need a synchronous pick-up.\n\n### P3 — Env flag parsing (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** Condition is `os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` (any non-empty string is truthy, including `\"0\"` and `\"false\"`).\n\n**Inferred:** `internal/run_mode.py` uses explicit false-token lists for similar flags; aligning would reduce misconfiguration.\n\n### P3 — No kick coalescing (inferred)\n\n**Inferred:** Each `kick_refresh_async()` call can spawn another daemon thread on web; writer path already had this pattern. Low risk for short reload work, but noisy under hot paths.\n\n## Owner rules / settled\n\n**Measured:** Writer-only publish path unchanged; web still cannot persist a built universe through this entry point.\n\n**Inferred (settled-check):** Split web/worker universe ownership in `ensure_background_refresh` / `ensure_universe_reader` is unchanged; this PR only opens `kick_refresh_async` for a flagged web path.\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone of `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` — membership grace and build logic are untouched.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAccept direction after a short comment documenting that `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` means “async disk reload on web, not writer refresh”, and confirm call sites tolerate async kick semantics (or call `reload_from_disk_if_stale` where synchronous freshness is required).",
