      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) at `8595d8fd288d013e8f2f75b16fb5c3bff29c0356`.\n\nThe diff adds one guard: on non-writer processes, `kick_refresh_async` only skips the early return when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, so the existing daemon kick thread can run instead of doing a synchronous `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` on the caller.\n\n**Why MODIFY (not FAIL):** Writer/publish rules are unchanged — **measured** `refresh_once()` still treats web as read-only and only reloads from disk. **Inferred** risks are contract clarity, not grace/expiry or overflow:\n\n1. **P2** — The kick thread still does not build or publish on web; it only async-reloads disk. That fits `is_universe_refresh_writer` but is easy to misread from the title; a one-line comment would help.\n2. **P2** — With the flag, kick returns before reload finishes, so callers must not assume the in-memory snapshot is updated immediately (base path blocked until reload completed).\n3. **P3** — Raw env truthiness (`\"false\"` / `\"0\"` still enable the path) vs patterns in `run_mode.py`.\n4. **P3** — Repeated kicks can spawn multiple short-lived threads (same pattern as the writer path).\n\nNo blocking tags (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` and `mc: missing`; the verdict comment was posted successfully via `post_verdict`. After the author addresses the notes (or Joshua accepts as-is), the gate should advance to Cursor/Ditto on the same head.",
