          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** PR 9403 changes only `SubnetUniverseProvider.reload_from_disk_if_stale` (web/reader path via `ensure_universe_reader`). The guard\n\n`if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"):`\n\nbecomes: reject non-dict; reject when `netuids` is missing/empty **unless** `status` is `\"ok\"` or `\"degraded\"`, then call `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)`.\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still sets `netuids` from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` only—it does not rebuild membership from `rows` or `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy; it was not updated in this diff.\n\n**Measured:** `load_membership_receipt()` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids`, not from rows.\n\n## Guard relaxation (required)\n\nThe relaxed line is intentional for **worker-published compacted** `subnet_universe.json` that may omit or empty the top-level `netuids` field while retaining `status` in `(\"ok\", \"degraded\")`. The old guard caused `reload_from_disk_if_stale` to keep the in-process snapshot when mtime advanced, so web readers never picked up a valid post-compaction file.\n\nRemaining rejection paths (**measured**): non-dict payload; empty/missing `netuids` when `status` is not `ok`/`degraded`; JSON/parse exceptions (unchanged).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Boot vs reload asymmetry (**measured**)\n\nA web process whose only on-disk LKG is compacted (no truthy `netuids`, `status` ok/degraded) still falls through to `emergency_registry` in `_load_initial_snapshot`. The new logic applies only after a **later** mtime bump on reload. Static compacted files after deploy do not get honored at boot—partial fix relative to the PR title.\n\n**Suggestion:** Mirror the same `status in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")` exception in `_load_initial_snapshot`, or centralize persist validation in one helper used by both paths.\n\n### P2 — Empty `netuids` after reload (**inferred**)\n\nIf compaction drops top-level `netuids` but keeps `rows`/`validity_map`, reload now succeeds but `snap.netuids` is empty while `snap.rows` may be non-empty. Receipt/scoring denominators keyed off `snap.netuids` can under-report membership until a full snapshot is written again. Not a float/NaN/overflow path; no cycle abort in refresh loop.\n\n**Suggestion:** When `netuids` is empty on load, derive membership from rows/validity_map inside `from_dict` or reject unless rows imply netuids.\n\n### P3 — Trust boundary (**inferred**)\n\nAny writer that can set `status: ok` with empty `netuids` on the persist file can force reload to adopt an empty membership tuple. Same disk trust as before; slightly wider accept window.\n\n## Extremes / entry point\n\nTraced reader entry: `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`. No numeric grace/overflow changes. `from_dict` still uses `int(n)` on netuid list elements—invalid values raise and hit the existing warning/retain-snapshot path (**inferred**, unchanged).\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nChange direction matches split worker/web persistence and fixes stale reader state after compaction **on reload**, but the diff is incomplete for cold start and for netuid/row consistency after `from_dict`. **MODIFY**, not FAIL—no measured never-expires, overflow, or refresh-loop abort.",
