      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259`.\n\nThe change correctly relaxes `reload_from_disk_if_stale` so web readers can adopt worker-compacted `subnet_universe.json` when `status` is `ok` or `degraded` even if top-level `netuids` is missing or empty—fixing the case where mtime moves but the old guard kept stale in-memory state.\n\n**Why MODIFY, not PASS**\n\n1. **Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids`, so a compacted on-disk LKG at process boot still becomes `emergency_registry`; only a later reload with a newer mtime picks up the file.\n2. **Measured + inferred:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` does not rebuild `netuids` from `rows`/`validity_map`, while `load_membership_receipt()` denominates from `snap.netuids`—reload can succeed with empty membership IDs but non-empty rows.\n\nThe review also documents the guard relaxation called out in the diff tooling (replacing the single `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` check with a status-aware rule).\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` / MC missing locally; the verdict post returned `posted: true`. Next gate step in production should be await Cursor/Ditto after MC is recorded on the PR.",
