            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the dict check from the membership check so disk files with falsy `netuids` but `status` in `(\"ok\", \"degraded\")` are loaded via `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` instead of keeping the in-memory snapshot.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Owner rule 1 / reader accepts zero-member persisted snapshot (**inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** At head, after the new guard, `from_dict` still does `netuids = tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))` and does not rebuild from `validity_map` keys. **Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy (unchanged).\n\n**Inferred:** A compacted or degraded on-disk payload with `status` `\"ok\"` or `\"degraded\"`, falsy `netuids`, and a non-empty `validity_map` (or rows) will replace a good in-memory `_snapshot` with `snap.netuids == ()`. Downstream: `get_netuids()` returns `[]`; `load_membership_receipt()` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids`; `get_lkg_or_emergency()` treats `not snap.netuids` as unusable. That is exactly the “reader accepts empty netuids and blanks membership” failure mode owner rule 1 forbids—the writer guard is not a defence on the reader path.\n\n**Inferred:** Under the *old* guard, the same disk file was ignored and the prior snapshot was retained—strictly safer for picks than this change.\n\nIf the intended compaction shape omits `netuids` but keeps `validity_map`, the reader should reconstruct membership (or reject the file) before assignment to `_snapshot`, not gate only on `status`.\n\n### P3 — Initial load vs reload mismatch (**measured**)\n\nFirst boot still emergency-falls back when `netuids` is missing; reload now accepts `ok`/`degraded` without `netuids`. Same on-disk artifact can be honored on reload but not on cold start.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial-review)\n\nNumeric edge cases (`1e308`, `NaN`, etc.) do not enter this JSON gate; no cycle-abort or float-overflow path touched.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced reader entry `ensure_universe_reader` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale` → `_snapshot` consumers | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1: reader must reject persisted snapshots with zero `netuids` | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture repo has no locks/roadmap/docs to search | — |\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMODIFY: either require non-empty `snap.netuids` (and/or rows) after `from_dict` before swapping `_snapshot`, or derive `netuids` from `validity_map` when the compact format omits the list; align `_load_initial_snapshot` with the same completeness rule.",
