            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the payload guard so a dict with falsy `netuids` but truthy `rows` still loads via `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`, while a dict with neither field still keeps the in-memory snapshot.\n\n## Guard relaxed (required)\n\n**Before:** `if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"): return self._snapshot`\n\n**After:** return early only when `payload` is not a dict, or when **both** `payload.get(\"netuids\")` and `payload.get(\"rows\")` are falsy.\n\n**Why this is safe here (inferred from head reads):**\n\n- **Real entry point:** web/readers call `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`; writers persist via `_atomic_persist` / `to_dict`, which always includes both keys when publishing a normal snapshot (**inferred** from `to_dict` at head).\n- **Mid-migration case:** `netuids` can be `[]` while `rows` is populated during a row-backed migration; the old guard treated `[]` like “missing” and skipped reload, leaving readers on stale disk mtime even after the worker updated the file (**inferred** from truthiness of `payload.get(\"netuids\")`).\n- **`from_dict` behavior (measured in file text):** builds `netuids` only from the `netuids` key and `rows` from `rows`; a rows-only payload yields empty `netuids` with non-empty `rows` — intentional for the PR title scenario.\n- **Downstream (inferred):** `get_pump_membership_rows()` serves `snap.rows`; `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still rejects `not snap.netuids` (emergency path). Coverage/scoring receipts use `snap.netuids` for `expected_netuids`, so empty netuids fail closed (`membership_empty` / gated admission in `snapshot_coverage.py`) rather than inventing membership from feed cardinality — consistent with owner fail-closed scoring.\n- **Extremes:** malformed `netuids` elements that make `int(n)` fail are caught by the existing `except` around load; reload returns prior `_snapshot` and logs — does not abort a refresh cycle. No float multiply / overflow path in this diff.\n- **Asymmetry (P3, non-blocking):** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids`; cold start during a rows-only on-disk file still falls through to `emergency_registry` until a later reload after mtime moves. This PR targets hot reader pickup, not boot (**inferred**).\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced reload guard → `from_dict` → `get_pump_membership_rows` / `get_lkg_or_emergency` / coverage receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Reader reload-only change; scoring fail-closed on empty membership; D5 row alignment | — |\n| settled-check | No fixture/docs lock re-litigating this guard; change matches stated migration intent | — |",
