      "finalText": "**MC verdict: PASS** posted for head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427` on [PR 9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404).\n\nThe diff only relaxes the reload guard in `reload_from_disk_if_stale` so a persisted dict with empty/falsy `netuids` but populated `rows` (mid-migration) still reloads. Payloads with neither `netuids` nor `rows` still keep the in-memory snapshot. **Inferred:** pump feeds can pick up row-backed disk state while membership/scoring stay fail-closed when `netuids` is empty (`get_lkg_or_emergency`, coverage admission). **P3 (non-blocking):** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids`, so cold start during a rows-only file is unchanged.\n\nGate `check_gate_state` still reports `next: review` and `mc: missing` in this fixture session even after a successful `post_verdict` post; the formal PASS comment should be on the PR. Next gate step in production is **await Cursor/Ditto** after MC is pinned at this SHA.",
