            "body": "MODIFY\n\n## Summary\nThe reload guard widens acceptance to any dict with a truthy `rows` key even when `netuids` is missing or empty (`[]`). **`UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still sets `netuids` only from `payload[\"netuids\"]`** (measured at head lines 483–484), so a row-backed file in that shape loads a snapshot with **zero `netuids`** while `rows` may be non-empty.\n\n## Entry point (measured)\nWeb/read path: `ensure_universe_reader()` → `SubnetUniverseProvider.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` → `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)` → `_snapshot` swap.\n\n## Adversarial case (inferred from code)\nDisk file: `{\"rows\": [{\"netuid\": 1, ...}, ...], \"netuids\": []}` or `netuids` omitted, mtime newer than `_disk_mtime`.\n- **Before PR:** `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` → keep in-memory LKG (no blanking).\n- **After PR:** `rows` truthy → `from_dict` → `netuids=()` → reader replaces LKG with an incomplete snapshot.\n\n## Why this blocks (owner rule 1, measured in system prompt)\nA persisted snapshot with empty/zero `netuids` is not complete; a reader that accepts it can replace a good snapshot with a blank membership surface. `get_netuids()` returns `[]` (measured lines 777–778). `get_lkg_or_emergency()` mitigates only that helper path (lines 780–784); **`get_snapshot()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` still expose the loaded object** — rows can be served while membership list is empty (lines 774–775, 822–826).\n\n## What would fix it\nKeep the split `isinstance` check, but after `from_dict` **reject unless membership is complete**: e.g. require non-empty `snap.netuids`, or derive `netuids` from `rows`/`validity_map` before accepting (same completeness bar as picks readers). Align `_load_initial_snapshot` (still requires truthy `netuids` only, lines 658–659) if row-backed LKG is intentional.\n\n## Non-blocking\n- Separating non-dict payload handling is a small clarity win (measured diff).\n- No float/overflow path touched.\n\n| Severity | Finding |\n| --- | --- |\n| P1 | Row-only / empty-`netuids` reload can blank shared universe membership (rule 1). |\n| P4 | Initial load vs reload guard mismatch. |\n\nLabels: **measured** = file text at head; **inferred** = reload timing with partial JSON on disk.",
