      "sessionId": "ses_b1d0c451e938fda8e1b744e5",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404) at head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427`.\n\n### Verdict: MODIFY (blocking: `poisons-later-row`)\n\nThe change loosens `reload_from_disk_if_stale` so a newer on-disk file is accepted when `rows` is present even if `netuids` is missing or empty. **`UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds `netuids` only from the top-level `netuids` field**, so a row-backed file with empty or absent `netuids` loads as **`netuids=()`** while `rows` may still be populated.\n\nThat conflicts with **owner rule 1**: the reader must not swap in a persisted snapshot with empty/zero `netuids`. Before this PR, falsy `netuids` kept the in-memory LKG; after it, the reader can replace a good universe with an incomplete one. `get_netuids()` goes empty; `get_lkg_or_emergency()` only helps callers that use that helper, not every `get_snapshot()` / pump row path.\n\n**Suggested fix:** keep the clearer non-`dict` handling, but after `from_dict` only commit the reload when membership is complete (non-empty `snap.netuids`, or derive `netuids` from `rows` / `validity_map` with the same completeness bar as picks readers). Optionally align `_load_initial_snapshot`, which still requires truthy `netuids` only.\n\n| Skill | Found |\n| --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Reader reload path; rows-without-netuids → empty membership |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 — incomplete snapshot accepted on reload |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture scope for this migration story |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after posting; follow `check_gate_state` on the live channel for the real next step.",
