t breaks `internal.run_mode` import would silently forfeit inline-web disk polling; same as pre-PR for that failure mode, not a publish leak.\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry point)\n\n`ensure_refresh_loop` → daemon thread → `_refresh_loop` → `refresh_once`. **Measured:** `refresh_once` first line gates publish on `is_universe_refresh_writer()`; non-writer path returns after disk reload. No numeric membership inputs change; no `never-expires` / overflow / cycle-abort / cross-row poison paths introduced by this diff.\n\n## Owner alignment\n\n**Inferred:** Preserving `is_universe_refresh_writer()` on publish matches the module docstring and D5 shared-universe ownership; extending loop **start** for inline-web disk follow is consistent with read-only web + worker publish, provided something actually calls `ensure_refresh_loop` on that VM.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nWire `ensure_background_refresh()` (or document and test the direct caller) so `inline_worker_expected()` web machines start the loop and get periodic `reload_from_disk_if_stale`, without opening publish on web.",
