      "sessionId": "ses_9b27fe9c43f770a1b84add03",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9405](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9405) at `9914127cfe0ef5c9ccbd731ae2647e6876cc77fd`.\n\n### What the change does (measured)\n`ensure_refresh_loop()` now starts the background thread when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, not only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true. CI/pytest still bail out first. Import failures fall back to the old writer-only gate.\n\n### Why MODIFY (not FAIL)\nThe guard change is aligned with split Fly v1 (web + sibling worker on shared disk): **measured** — `refresh_once()` still refuses to build/publish on non-writer processes and only runs `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`, so owner rule 4 holds.\n\n**P2 (inferred + measured in this diff):** `ensure_background_refresh()` still calls `ensure_universe_reader()` on the non-writer path and never calls `ensure_refresh_loop()`. With only `internal/subnet_universe.py` changed, INLINE_WORKER web may still never start the 300s reload loop unless something else calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` directly. Suggested follow-up: in the `else` branch, when `inline_worker_expected()`, also start the loop (after the one-shot reader reload).\n\nNo blocking categories (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\nGate `next` remains `review` in the fixture snapshot; MC verdict is on the PR. Next step per gate order is Cursor review at this head.",
