            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line guard change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: accept persisted payloads when `rows` is non-empty even if `netuids` is cleared/empty.\n\n## Guard removed (required explanation)\n\n**Removed:** `if isinstance(payload, dict) and payload.get(\"netuids\"):`\n\n**Replaced with:** `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`.\n\n**Intent (inferred):** Avoid `emergency_registry` on startup when disk still has row payloads but the `netuids` list was cleared.\n\n**Risk (inferred from code):** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` does **not** rebuild `netuids` from `rows` or `validity_map`; it sets `netuids` from the payload list only (`payload.get(\"netuids\") or []`). The snapshot can therefore load with **empty `netuids` and non-empty `rows`/`validity_map`**, which downstream logic was not written to treat as a consistent LKG.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Refresh can discard row-only LKG; shrink guard bypass (poisons-later-row)\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` only (not from `rows` or `validity_map` keys). `_shrink_allowed` compares `set(prior.netuids) - set(built.netuids)`; when `prior.netuids` is empty, shrink is vacuously allowed.\n\n**Measured:** Empty-membership / hold paths gate on `prior and prior.netuids` (e.g. retain prior on empty resolution). With cleared `netuids` but intact `rows`, those branches do not run, so a refresh can publish a new snapshot that **drops persisted row membership** without going through 48h grace removal on the prior netuids.\n\n**Inferred:** This is worse than rejecting the file (old guard → `emergency_registry`): the process keeps row data in memory briefly, then the worker refresh cycle can overwrite it with a smaller/empty membership that later readers consume.\n\n### P2 — Reader reload still rejects the same shape\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")`. Web/read-only processes will **not** pick up worker-published files that match the PR’s target shape after mtime advances.\n\n### P2 — `get_lkg_or_emergency` still treats empty `netuids` as unusable\n\n**Measured:** `if snap.status == \"emergency_registry\" or not snap.netuids: return emergency_registry(...)`. Loaded row-only LKG remains “no usable snapshot” on that entry point even when `_load_initial_snapshot` succeeds.\n\n### P3 — Scoring receipt ignores rows for membership denominator\n\n**Measured:** `load_membership_receipt` builds `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` only. Empty `netuids` → empty expected set while `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still return `snap.rows` (**inferred** pump vs scoring divergence).\n\n## Recommended fix (minimal direction)\n\n1. On load (in `from_dict` or immediately after), **reconcile `netuids`** from `validity_map` keys and/or `_netuid_of` on `rows` when the stored list is empty.\n2. Apply the **same** accept predicate to `reload_from_disk_if_stale`.\n3. Align `get_lkg_or_emergency` / hold-empty logic with the reconciled membership (or document and test that row-only files are display-only until refresh).\n4. Add a regression test: persisted `{netuids: [], rows: [...], validity_map: {...}}` survives `refresh_once` without silent shrink.\n\n## Owner rules touched\n\n**Measured:** Comments require 48h grace and chain-driven removal via `_eligible_for_removal` / `_shrink_allowed` on **`prior.netuids`**. Accepting inconsistent disk state without reconciling `netuids` undermines those guards for the row-only shape this PR enables.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\nNo float/JSON numeric edge case in this diff; the relevant “extreme” is **empty `netuids` + full `rows`/`validity_map`**, which the change now admits at startup and feeds into `refresh_once` → `_publish`.",
