      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe one-line change relaxes the LKG load guard so payloads with cleared `netuids` but non-empty `rows` are accepted in `_load_initial_snapshot`. That guard removal is reasonable only if membership is reconciled on load; **measured** in code, `from_dict` still sets `netuids` only from the payload list, while `SnapshotBuilder.build` and `_shrink_allowed` key off `prior.netuids`. **Inferred**, a row-only LKG can therefore pass startup, then lose coverage on the next worker refresh without the usual 48h shrink guard firing — declared as blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nAlso **measured**: `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `netuids`, and `get_lkg_or_emergency` still treats empty `netuids` as unusable, so the PR only partially addresses the title scenario.\n\nRecommended direction in the verdict: reconcile `netuids` from `rows`/`validity_map` on load, mirror the guard in reload, add a regression test around `refresh_once`. Gate `next` in the fixture still reads `review`; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow your channel’s gate after MC.",
